window.SM_KNOWLEDGE = {"气温 Ta":{"unit":"℃","desc":"距地 1.5 m、通风遮阳条件下的空气温度，是热环境的基准量，也是全部热舒适指标的输入之一。","ranges":[["22–26 ℃","中性（夏季户外舒适）","ok"],["26–28 ℃","微暖，可接受","ok"],["28–32 ℃","轻度热应激","warn"],["32–35 ℃","中度热应激","warn"],[">35 ℃","重度；连续 3 日即构成热浪","bad"],["夜间 >28 ℃","无缓解型热浪，人体夜间无法恢复","bad"],["8–16 ℃","冬季可接受区间（亚热带城市研究中性区间参考）","info"]],"targets":[["夏季停留区（荫下）","≤30 ℃"],["冬季室外可停留","≥10 ℃ 且避风"]],"why":"它是 UTCI / PET / WBGT 的共同输入；任何一项测偏，三个指标一起偏。","how":"把 Ta 当背景条件，而不是干预目标 —— 设计无法显著降低气温，能完全控制的是辐射（遮荫）。所以看到 Ta 要联想到「转向 Tmrt 与遮荫份额」。这是 Designing Shade 的核心论断。","watch":"传感器不戴辐射防护罩会高估 3–5 ℃；须远离空调外机与排风口。","cases":["Designing Shade"],"srcs":[["Designing Shade（Or Aleksandrowicz 访谈）","https://medium.com/urban-ai/designing-shade-7f6a8f66abed"]],"unitEn":"℃","titleEn":"Air Temperature (Ta)","descEn":"Air temperature at 1.5 m under ventilated, shaded conditions. The baseline of the thermal environment and one of the inputs to every thermal comfort index.","rangesEn":["Neutral (comfortable outdoors in summer)","Slightly warm, acceptable","Mild heat stress","Moderate heat stress","Severe; three consecutive days constitutes a heatwave","Nocturnal, no-relief heatwave — the body cannot recover overnight","Acceptable winter range (sub-tropical city reference)"],"targetsEn":[["Summer seating area (shaded)","≤30 °C"],["Usable outdoors in winter","≥10 °C and wind-sheltered"]],"whyEn":"It is the common input to UTCI, PET and WBGT. Any error in measuring Ta skews all three indices together.","howEn":"Treat Ta as a background condition, not a design target. Design cannot meaningfully lower air temperature; what it can control completely is radiation (shade). So Ta should route you towards Tmrt and shade fraction. This is the core argument of Designing Shade.","watchEn":"An unshielded sensor over-reads by 3–5 °C; keep it away from air-conditioner outlets and exhaust vents.","srcsEn":["Designing Shade (interview with Or Aleksandrowicz)"],"casesEn":["Designing Shade"]},"平均辐射温度 Tmrt":{"unit":"℃","desc":"综合六个方向辐射得热后的人体等效辐射温度，衡量「被晒与被烤」的程度，而不是空气有多热。","ranges":[["<35 ℃","辐射环境温和","ok"],["35–50 ℃","辐射负荷明显","warn"],[">50 ℃","无遮挡硬质铺装上的常见值，体感远高于气温","bad"]],"targets":[["夏季停留区","降低 10 ℃ 以上（遮荫即可达成）"]],"why":"在烈日下的街道，Tmrt 常常比 Ta 高 20 ℃ 以上 —— 人体感受到的热主要来自辐射，不是气温。","how":"这是空间设计最有杠杆的物理量：加一层遮荫，Tmrt 立刻下降，而 Ta 几乎不变。可动遮阳、树冠、膜结构、骑楼都在作用于此。也是「同一气温下，有荫与无荫体感差一个等级」的原因。","watch":"由六向辐射表或黑球温度计测得，设备贵；可用 3D 模型 + 太阳轨迹模拟替代实测。","cases":["Madinah Piazza Shading","Cooling Path"],"srcs":[["ISO 7726 热环境仪器与测量方法",""]],"unitEn":"℃","titleEn":"Mean Radiant Temperature (Tmrt)","descEn":"The equivalent radiant temperature of a person after integrating radiation gain from six directions. It measures being baked rather than how hot the air is.","rangesEn":["Mild radiant environment","Noticeable radiant load","Common value on unshaded hard paving; felt far hotter than air temperature"],"targetsEn":[["Summer seating area","Reduce by more than 10 °C (achievable with shade alone)"]],"whyEn":"On a sunlit street Tmrt is often more than 20 °C above Ta. The heat people feel comes mainly from radiation, not from air temperature.","howEn":"This is the physical quantity with the greatest design leverage: add one layer of shade and Tmrt drops immediately while Ta barely moves. Movable shading, tree canopy, tensile membranes and arcades all act on it. It also explains why, at the same air temperature, a shaded and an unshaded spot feel a whole grade apart.","watchEn":"Measured with a six-direction radiometer or globe thermometer — expensive equipment. A 3D model plus solar-path simulation is an acceptable substitute.","srcsEn":["ISO 7726, thermal environment instruments and methods"],"casesEn":["Madinah Piazza Shading","Cooling Path"]},"遮荫份额":{"unit":"%","desc":"步行空间上被建筑或树木阴影覆盖的面积比例。只看人的通行空间，不看城市绿化覆盖率。","ranges":[["<20 %","遮荫严重不足","bad"],["20–40 %","偏少","warn"],["40–60 %","中等，可作为改善目标","warn"],[">60 %","良好","ok"]],"targets":[["街区改善目标","遮荫份额 ≥50 %"],["优先对象","通往公交站与学校的步行路径"]],"why":"它把「遮荫」从形容词变成了数字，而且可以排序 —— 有限资源下决定先做哪一段。","how":"用 LiDAR 或摄影测量的建筑与树木 3D 数据 + 临界日太阳轨迹做射线求交，不需要现场传感器。北半球临界日取 8 月 6 日；5 月初太阳角与之相同，可作第二时点对照。","watch":"必须限定在步行空间上，否则与绿化覆盖率混为一谈，会得出「这个城市很绿所以不缺荫」的错误结论。","cases":["Designing Shade","Shaded Politics"],"srcs":[["BDAR 遮荫地图","https://oraleks.net.technion.ac.il/en/shade-maps/"]],"unitEn":"%","titleEn":"Shade Fraction","descEn":"The share of pedestrian space covered by building or tree shadow. Only the space people walk through counts, not citywide green coverage.","rangesEn":["Severely under-shaded","Low","Moderate — a reasonable improvement target","Good"],"targetsEn":[["Neighbourhood improvement target","Shade fraction ≥50 %"],["Priority","Walking routes to bus stops and schools"]],"whyEn":"It turns shade from an adjective into a number, and a number can be ranked — which decides which segment to fix first when resources are limited.","howEn":"Use LiDAR or photogrammetric 3D data of buildings and trees plus the solar path of a critical day to run ray-casting. No field sensors needed. In the northern hemisphere the critical day is 6 August; early May has the same solar altitude and can serve as a second control point.","watchEn":"Must be limited to pedestrian space. Otherwise it gets confused with green coverage and yields the false conclusion that a green city needs no more shade.","srcsEn":["BDAR shade maps"],"casesEn":["Designing Shade","Shaded Politics"]},"相对湿度 RH":{"unit":"%","desc":"空气中水汽的饱和程度。它决定蒸发降温能不能用、人体出汗能不能散热。","ranges":[["<30 %","干燥，蒸发降温效率最高","ok"],["30–60 %","蒸发降温有效（效率随湿度上升下降）","ok"],["60–80 %","蒸发降温效果明显减弱","warn"],[">80 %","蒸发降温基本失效，且闷热加重","bad"],["露点 >24 ℃","人体散热困难，体感显著恶化","bad"]],"targets":[["喷雾降温启用门槛","RH <70 % 才开；>80 % 必须停"],["上海梅雨期","以通风与遮荫替代蒸发路线"]],"why":"同温度下，湿度决定体感是「干热可忍」还是「闷热难当」；也直接决定降温手段的可用性。","how":"这是选路线的前置判断：先测 RH，再决定用蒸发还是用遮荫与通风。上海梅雨期 RH 常在 80 % 以上，水景与喷雾不仅无效，还会把闷热加重 —— 这一条必须写进设计前提。","watch":"长期高湿环境传感器读数易漂移，需定期校准。","cases":["Cloud Cast","Wiesbaden 广场喷雾"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"%","titleEn":"Relative Humidity (RH)","descEn":"The degree of saturation of the air with water vapour. It decides whether evaporative cooling can be used at all, and whether the body can shed heat by sweating.","rangesEn":["Dry; evaporative cooling at its most efficient","Evaporative cooling effective (efficiency falls as humidity rises)","Evaporative cooling markedly weakened","Evaporative cooling essentially fails and stickiness worsens","Human heat loss becomes difficult; felt conditions deteriorate sharply"],"targetsEn":[["Misting trigger threshold","Run only when RH <70 %; stop above 80 %"],["Shanghai plum-rain season","Use ventilation and shade instead of the evaporative route"]],"whyEn":"At the same temperature, humidity decides whether the heat is dry and tolerable or humid and oppressive. It also directly decides which cooling measures remain available.","howEn":"This is the upstream decision that picks the route: measure RH first, then choose evaporation or shade-and-ventilation. During Shanghai's plum-rain season RH is often above 80 %, where water features and misting are not only ineffective but make the mugginess worse. This belongs in the design brief as a precondition.","watchEn":"Sensors drift in long-term humid conditions; calibrate regularly.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Cloud Cast","Wiesbaden 广场喷雾"]},"风速 v":{"unit":"m/s","desc":"1.5 m 行人高度的平均风速。既影响热舒适（有风散热），也影响安全感（风大不稳）。","ranges":[["<0.2 m/s","静风，夏季闷热，污染物易滞留","warn"],["0.2–1.5 m/s","舒适区，夏季最理想","ok"],["1.5–2.2 m/s","停留区上限，再大影响坐憩","warn"],["2.2–5 m/s","步行可接受，坐憩不适","warn"],[">5 m/s（阵风 >10.8）","影响步行稳定性，需挡风","bad"]],"targets":[["夏季停留区","0.5–1.5 m/s（要风）"],["冬季停留区","≤1.5 m/s（避风）"]],"why":"它是唯一「夏天想要、冬天想躲」的物理量，所以必须做成可调或可拆。","how":"夏冬诉求相反 → 构件必须可变：可调导风板、可拆透明风挡、季节模式切换。设计时先查场地盛行风向与街道走向夹角，夹角 ≤30° 时风能顺着街道进来。","watch":"街谷内风场高度不均，单点测量不具代表性，布点前应先用 CFD 判断。","cases":["香港空气流通评估 AVA","大学路冬季透明风挡"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"m/s","titleEn":"Wind Speed (v)","descEn":"Mean wind speed at 1.5 m pedestrian height. It affects thermal comfort (wind sheds heat) and also perceived safety (strong wind destabilises).","rangesEn":["Still air; muggy in summer and pollutants linger","Comfort zone, ideal in summer","Upper limit for seating areas; above this sitting suffers","Acceptable for walking, uncomfortable for sitting","Walking stability affected; windbreak needed"],"targetsEn":[["Summer seating area","0.5–1.5 m/s (wind wanted)"],["Winter seating area","≤1.5 m/s (wind avoided)"]],"whyEn":"It is the only physical quantity that is wanted in summer and avoided in winter, so it must be made adjustable or removable.","howEn":"Opposite summer and winter requirements mean the component must be variable: adjustable wind deflectors, removable transparent screens, seasonal mode switching. Before designing, check the angle between prevailing wind direction and street axis — up to about 30° the wind still travels along the street.","watchEn":"Wind fields inside a street canyon are highly uneven; a single point measurement is not representative. Use CFD before placing sensors.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Hong Kong Air Ventilation Assessment (AVA)","大学路冬季透明风挡"]},"PM2.5 / PM10":{"unit":"µg/m³","desc":"空气动力学当量直径小于 2.5 µm / 10 µm 的颗粒物浓度。","ranges":[["≤35 µg/m³","优（国标一级日均参考）","ok"],["35–75 µg/m³","良（国标二级限值 75）","warn"],[">75 µg/m³","超标，敏感人群应减少户外停留","bad"],["WHO 参考","年均 5 µg/m³ —— 全球极少城市达标","info"]],"targets":[["步行带暴露削减","相对浓度下降 ≥30 %"]],"why":"街道峡谷底部是污染物最容易积聚的地方，而行人正好呼吸在这个高度。","how":"三条有效路径：① 拉开源—受体距离（绿篱或绿墙设在路缘与步行道之间）；② 提高街道底面孔隙率（柱廊、通透底层）改善扩散；③ 光催化（TiO₂）铺装或立面降解 NOx 与 O₃。注意：密植大树冠在繁忙街道会困住污染物，与「增加绿量」的直觉相反。","watch":"湿度对光散射读数干扰大；低成本传感器漂移明显，需月度标定。","cases":["Smog Free Tower","CityTree / CityBreeze"],"srcs":[["绿篱屏障实测：近校环境叶面 PM2.5 负载 −82 %",""]],"unitEn":"µg/m³","titleEn":"PM2.5 / PM10","descEn":"Mass concentration of particulate matter with an aerodynamic diameter below 2.5 µm / 10 µm.","rangesEn":["Excellent (reference for the national Grade I daily mean)","Good (national Grade II limit is 75)","Above limit; sensitive groups should reduce outdoor time","WHO reference — almost no city worldwide meets it"],"targetsEn":[["Exposure reduction along walking corridors","Relative concentration down ≥30 %"]],"whyEn":"The bottom of a street canyon is where pollutants accumulate most, and it is exactly the height at which pedestrians breathe.","howEn":"Three effective routes: (1) increase source–receptor distance by putting hedges or green walls between the kerb and the footway; (2) raise ground-level porosity (colonnades, permeable ground floors) to improve dispersion; (3) photocatalytic (TiO2) paving or facades to break down NOx and O3. Caution: densely planted large canopies on a busy street trap pollutants — the opposite of the greenery-equals-good instinct.","watchEn":"Humidity interferes strongly with light-scattering readings; low-cost sensors drift noticeably and need monthly calibration.","srcsEn":["Measured hedge barrier study: leaf-surface PM2.5 load −82 % near a school"],"casesEn":["Smog Free Tower","CityTree / CityBreeze"]},"等效声级 LAeq":{"unit":"dB(A)","desc":"按能量平均的等效连续 A 计权声级，反映一段时间内的噪声暴露水平。","ranges":[["<55 dB(A)","安静（居住区夜间参考）","ok"],["55–65 dB(A)","一般交谈不受影响","ok"],["65–75 dB(A)","需提高音量交谈","warn"],[">75 dB(A)","交通干道常见值，长时间暴露有害","bad"]],"targets":[["停留区","≤65 dB(A)"],["水声掩蔽","掩蔽声级略高于交通噪声最有效"]],"why":"噪声是街道最普遍却最少被设计的胁迫因子，而它直接决定人愿不愿意停留。","how":"① 多孔透水铺装可降轮胎噪声 2–8 dB；② 绿化屏障结合起伏地形；③ 用水声掩蔽 —— 掩蔽比降噪更可行，因为降 5 dB 要付很高代价，而引入愉悦声源只需一个水景。","watch":"风雨与落叶会造成假信号，设备需防风雨罩与防盗。","cases":["复合屏障单元"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"dB(A)","titleEn":"Equivalent Sound Level (LAeq)","descEn":"Energy-averaged equivalent continuous A-weighted sound level, expressing noise exposure over a period.","rangesEn":["Quiet (reference for residential night-time)","Normal conversation unaffected","Conversation requires raised voice","Common on arterial roads; harmful over long exposure"],"targetsEn":[["Seating area","≤65 dB(A)"],["Water sound masking","Masker slightly louder than the traffic noise works best"]],"whyEn":"Noise is the most widespread and least designed-for stressor on streets, yet it directly decides whether people are willing to stay.","howEn":"(1) Porous permeable paving reduces tyre noise by 2–8 dB; (2) green barriers combined with undulating ground; (3) water sound masking — masking is more feasible than reduction, because cutting 5 dB is expensive while adding a pleasant source costs one water feature.","watchEn":"Wind, rain and leaves cause false signals; equipment needs a weather shield and anti-theft fixing.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["复合屏障单元"]},"降雨强度":{"unit":"mm/h","desc":"单位时间的降雨量；与累积雨量、重现期共同决定雨洪设计标准。","ranges":[["<2.5 mm/h","小雨","ok"],["2.5–8 mm/h","中雨","warn"],["8–20 mm/h","大雨","warn"],[">20 mm/h","暴雨，短历时即可能积水","bad"]],"targets":[["设计校核","T10 重现期（气候砖按 2100 年 T10 校核）"],["退水时间","雨后 30 min 内无积水"]],"why":"气候变化下短历时强降雨频率上升，而街道是最先积水的地方。","how":"按「蓄—滞—渗—净—用」五字诀设计：下沉水池与蓄水模块、透水铺装、明沟导流、雨水花园净化、回用灌溉。空间上做成「干湿两态」——平时是球场，雨时是水池，一笔投资两套功能。","watch":"泥沙与落叶易堵塞探头；污浊水体使光学与超声失准，优选压力式水位计。","cases":["Watersquare Benthemplein","Klimaflisen 气候砖","深圳中康路海绵化"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"mm/h","titleEn":"Rainfall Intensity","descEn":"Rainfall per unit time. Together with cumulative rainfall and return period it sets the stormwater design standard.","rangesEn":["Light rain","Moderate rain","Heavy rain","Cloudburst; ponding possible within a short duration"],"targetsEn":[["Design check","T10 return period (climate tiles are checked against a 2100 T10 event)"],["Recession time","No ponding within 30 min after rain"]],"whyEn":"Short-duration intense rainfall is becoming more frequent under climate change, and streets are the first places to flood.","howEn":"Design on the five verbs: store, detain, infiltrate, cleanse, reuse — sunken basins and storage modules, permeable paving, open channels, rain gardens, irrigation reuse. Spatially this becomes a dry-wet dual state: a ball court in dry weather, a basin in rain, one investment for two functions.","watchEn":"Silt and leaves block probes; turbid water defeats optical and ultrasonic sensors, so pressure-type level sensors are preferred.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Watersquare Benthemplein","Klimaflisen Climate Tile","深圳中康路海绵化"]},"天空视角因子 SVF":{"unit":"0–1","desc":"从某点向上看到的天空半球比例。SVF 越小说明被建筑与树冠遮挡越多。","ranges":[["夏季 SVF >0.2","与热舒适正相关（更开敞、通风好）","ok"],["夏季 SVF <0.2","辐射被困、通风差，热压力高","bad"],["冬季 SVF ≤0.4","与热舒适负相关（太阳得热不足）","bad"],["转折点约 0.51","新加坡高密区 UTCI 由降转升的经验阈值","info"]],"targets":[["夏季","避免过低 SVF（<0.2）形成辐射陷阱"],["冬季","保证足够天空开敞以获取日照"]],"why":"它是街道几何的单一指标，却能同时预测夏季与冬季的热表现。","how":"用鱼眼镜头拍摄或 3D 模型做半球积分即可算得，无需现场传感器。SVF 与遮荫份额要配合看：SVF 低不等于有荫（可能只是被高楼遮住而形成了风影与辐射陷阱）。","watch":"SVF 与热舒适的关系非线性，且夏冬方向相反 —— 不存在一个全年最优值，只能靠可动构件折中。","cases":["香港 AVA"],"srcs":[["SVF 与校园街道热舒适阈值研究（Buildings 2025）","https://www.mdpi.com/2075-5309/15/22/4121"]],"unitEn":"0–1","titleEn":"Sky View Factor (SVF)","descEn":"The proportion of the sky hemisphere visible from a given point. A smaller SVF means more occlusion by buildings and canopy.","rangesEn":["Positively correlated with thermal comfort in summer (more open, better ventilated)","Radiation trapped and ventilation poor; high heat stress","Negatively correlated with winter thermal comfort (insufficient solar gain)","Empirical turning point in high-density Singapore, where UTCI shifts from falling to rising"],"targetsEn":[["Summer","Avoid very low SVF (<0.2), which forms a radiation trap"],["Winter","Keep enough sky openness to gain sunlight"]],"whyEn":"It is a single indicator of street geometry that nonetheless predicts both summer and winter thermal performance.","howEn":"Compute with a fisheye photograph or hemispherical integration on a 3D model; no field sensors needed. Read SVF together with shade fraction: a low SVF does not mean shade — it may simply be occlusion by tall buildings, creating a wind shadow and a radiation trap.","watchEn":"The relationship between SVF and thermal comfort is non-linear and reverses between summer and winter. There is no single year-round optimum, only a compromise through movable components.","srcsEn":["SVF and thermal comfort thresholds on campus streets (Buildings 2025)"],"casesEn":["香港 AVA"]},"湿球黑球温度 WBGT":{"unit":"℃","desc":"由自然湿球、黑球、干球温度加权合成的热应力指数，广泛用于户外作业与运动的暴露上限。","ranges":[["<28 ℃","低风险","ok"],["28–31 ℃","中等风险，需控制活动强度","warn"],["31–33 ℃","高风险","bad"],[">33 ℃","极高风险，应避免户外作业","bad"]],"targets":[["夏季正午户外活动","控制在 31 ℃ 以下"]],"why":"它是「能不能让人在这个时间段待在户外」的判定依据，比气温更贴近人体真实负荷。","how":"室外按 0.7 × 自然湿球 + 0.2 × 黑球 + 0.1 × 干球加权。三件套仪器简单耐用，适合作为现场长期监测的锚点设备。","watch":"它不包含风速的完整影响，强通风条件下会高估热应力；精细研究宜与 UTCI 并用。","cases":["札幌冬季融雪对策"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"℃","titleEn":"Wet Bulb Globe Temperature (WBGT)","descEn":"A heat-stress index combining natural wet-bulb, globe and dry-bulb temperature, widely used as an exposure limit for outdoor work and sport.","rangesEn":["Low risk","Moderate risk; control activity intensity","High risk","Extreme risk; avoid outdoor work"],"targetsEn":[["Midday outdoor activity in summer","Keep below 31 °C"]],"whyEn":"It is the basis for deciding whether people can be outdoors at a given time of day, and it tracks real human load better than air temperature.","howEn":"Outdoors, weight 0.7 × natural wet-bulb + 0.2 × globe + 0.1 × dry-bulb. The three-part instrument is simple and durable, well suited as an anchor device for long-term on-site monitoring.","watchEn":"It does not fully capture the effect of wind speed and over-estimates heat stress under strong ventilation; finer studies should pair it with UTCI.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Sapporo Winter Snow-Melting Measures"]},"街道高宽比 AR":{"unit":"H/W","desc":"临街建筑平均高度与街道宽度之比，刻画街道峡谷的「深浅」。","ranges":[["<0.5","开敞，通风好但缺少遮荫","warn"],["0.5–1.0","较舒适，兼顾通风与遮蔽","ok"],["1.0–2.0","典型街谷，午后辐射被困","warn"],[">2.0","深街谷，流场复杂、污染物易滞留","bad"]],"targets":[["改造可行性","AR >2 的深街谷不宜再加设密植屏障"],["导风","主要街段与盛行风平行或夹角 ≤30°"]],"why":"AR 是决定街谷能否自我通风的几何参数，也是判断「加构件会不会帮倒忙」的前提。","how":"AR 大（深而窄）→ 风难穿透、污染物易滞留，需要靠风塔、转角倒角、地面孔隙率改善；AR 小（宽而浅）→ 通风好但缺荫，应优先补遮荫。一个参数就能定下改造方向。","watch":"AR >2 时流场复杂，工程经验不再适用，加屏障前必须做流体模拟。","cases":["香港空气流通评估 AVA","岭南冷巷"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"H/W","titleEn":"Street Aspect Ratio (AR)","descEn":"The ratio of average building height to street width, characterising how deep the street canyon is.","rangesEn":["Open; well ventilated but under-shaded","Comfortable; balances ventilation and shelter","Typical canyon; afternoon radiation trapped","Deep canyon; complex flow and pollutants linger"],"targetsEn":[["Retrofit feasibility","Avoid adding dense barriers in canyons with AR >2"],["Wind guidance","Main street segment parallel to prevailing wind, or within 30°"]],"whyEn":"AR is the geometric parameter that decides whether a canyon can ventilate itself, and the precondition for judging whether an added component will help or backfire.","howEn":"High AR (deep and narrow): wind struggles to penetrate and pollutants linger — improve with wind towers, chamfered corners and ground-level porosity. Low AR (wide and shallow): good ventilation but no shade — prioritise shade. One parameter settles the retrofit direction.","watchEn":"Above AR 2 the flow field is complex and engineering rules of thumb no longer apply; run fluid simulation before adding barriers.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Hong Kong Air Ventilation Assessment (AVA)","岭南冷巷"]},"竖向透明风挡":{"unit":"m / 块","desc":"设在外摆或停留区边缘的透明挡风板，挡风但保留视线与日照。","ranges":[["高度 0.9–1.2 m","挡人腿脚处的下掠风，不遮视线","ok"],["高度 1.5 m 以上","挡风效果好但影响坐憩视线","warn"],["透光率 ≥70 %","不遮挡商业展示面与内部视线","ok"]],"targets":[["夏冬策略","冬季安装、夏季拆除（可逆）"],["成效参照","大学路试点 2024.12–2025.3 销售额同比 +24 %，最冷 2 月近 +40 %"]],"why":"它是「冬夏诉求相反」这条矛盾最直接、最便宜的一个答案：拆下来就变回夏天要的穿堂风。","how":"布点先判断是「冷风问题」还是「缺日照问题」：有风无风都冷 → 缺日照，加风挡无用；有风时明显更冷 → 加风挡。风挡必须可逆安装，避免夏天反向受害。","watch":"不得侵占疏散净宽；不得遮挡商业展示面与标识，这是市容管理的硬边界。","cases":["上海大学路外摆"],"srcs":[["中国新闻网：大学路外摆与冬季风挡","https://m.chinanews.com/wap/detail/cht/zw/10473388.shtml"]],"unitEn":"m / panel","titleEn":"Vertical Transparent Wind Screen","descEn":"A transparent wind screen at the edge of a spill-out or seating area. It blocks wind while preserving sightlines and sunlight.","rangesEn":["Blocks the downwash at leg height without blocking sightlines","Good wind blocking but obstructs the seated view","Does not block shopfront display or interior sightlines"],"targetsEn":[["Summer-winter strategy","Install in winter, remove in summer (reversible)"],["Evidence","Daxue Road pilot Dec 2024 – Mar 2025: sales +24 % year on year, nearly +40 % in the coldest February"]],"whyEn":"It is the cheapest and most direct answer to the opposite-demands problem: take it down and the through-draught wanted in summer returns.","howEn":"First diagnose whether the problem is cold wind or lack of sun. Cold whether windy or not means insufficient solar gain, and a screen will not help; markedly colder when windy means a screen will. Screens must be reversibly installed so they do not cause harm in summer.","watchEn":"Must not encroach on evacuation width, nor block shopfronts and signage — this is a hard boundary in street-management rules.","srcsEn":["China News Service: Daxue Road spill-out seating and winter wind screens"],"casesEn":["上海大学路外摆"]},"太阳反射率 albedo":{"unit":"0–1","desc":"表面对太阳辐射的反射比例。反射越高，表面吸收得越少，白天升温越慢。","ranges":[["0.05–0.10","深色沥青，表面温度可达 65 ℃ 以上","bad"],["0.10–0.20","常规混凝土","warn"],["0.20–0.40","浅色铺装，明显降温","ok"],[">0.40","高反射冷铺装，降温最强","ok"],[">0.158（湿热高密区）","反成净增温 —— 短波反射直射人体","bad"]],"targets":[["表面温度","每提高 albedo 0.1，约降 4 ℃"],["正确做法","先加遮荫，再提高反射率"]],"why":"它是最便宜的降温手段（换铺装或刷涂层），但也是唯一「用过头会反效果」的物理量。","how":"次序很关键：**先遮后反**。有遮荫时（SVF 低），反射光被挡住，只留下降温收益；无遮荫的开敞步行区（SVF 高）提高反射率，会把短波反射到行人身上，净效果是更热。湿热高密地区这一阈值约为 0.158，已实测到反效果。","watch":"高反射还会带来眩光，宜用逆反射材料（把阳光近似垂直反射回天，而非水平射向人眼）。","cases":["Cool Pavement 洛杉矶 / 凤凰城"],"srcs":[["EPA 冷铺装使用指南","https://www.epa.gov/heatislands/using-cool-pavements-reduce-heat-islands"],["高密湿热城市 albedo 阈值研究","https://arxiv.org/html/2604.22433v2"]],"unitEn":"0–1","titleEn":"Solar Reflectance (Albedo)","descEn":"The fraction of solar radiation reflected by a surface. The higher the reflection, the less the surface absorbs and the slower it heats during the day.","rangesEn":["Dark asphalt; surface temperature can exceed 65 °C","Conventional concrete","Light-coloured paving; marked cooling","High-reflectance cool pavement; strongest cooling","Becomes net warming — shortwave reflects straight onto people"],"targetsEn":[["Surface temperature","Roughly 4 °C lower per 0.1 increase in albedo"],["Correct sequence","Add shade first, then raise reflectance"]],"whyEn":"It is the cheapest cooling measure (swap paving or apply a coating), but also the only physical quantity that backfires when overdone.","howEn":"Sequence matters: shade first, reflectance second. With shade (low SVF) the reflected light is blocked and only the cooling gain remains; on open unshaded footways (high SVF) raising reflectance bounces shortwave onto pedestrians and the net effect is hotter. In hot-humid high-density districts the threshold is about 0.158, and a net warming effect has been measured.","watchEn":"High reflectance also causes glare; retroreflective materials (which send sunlight almost vertically back to the sky rather than horizontally at eye level) are preferable.","srcsEn":["EPA guide to using cool pavements to reduce heat islands","Study of albedo thresholds in dense hot-humid cities"],"casesEn":["Cool Pavement 洛杉矶 / 凤凰城"]},"相变温度与相变潜热":{"unit":"℃ / kJ·kg⁻¹","desc":"材料在相变温度附近吸放热而温度基本不变的能力，相当于一个「热的缓冲器」。","ranges":[["相变点在 24–28 ℃","适合上海夏季路面，白天融化吸热","ok"],["有效时段 7:00–10:00","实测降温主要发生在此窗口","info"],["降温幅度 2.9–8.3 ℃","相变铺装实测表面温度降幅","ok"],["超过一定掺量后","再增加掺量收益不再明显","warn"]],"targets":[["适用场景","昼夜温差大、白天迅速升温的硬质面"]],"why":"它能把「白天吸热、夜间放热」的过程平缓掉，削掉温度峰值，而不是整体降温。","how":"用在铺装面层或砂浆里。要按使用时段的温度曲线选相变点：相变点必须落在你要削峰的那个时段的气温区间内，否则整块材料在「睡觉」。","watch":"只在相变温度区间内有效，其余时段与普通材料无异；夜间会放热，需与夜间通风配合。","cases":["相变铺装研究（Cool Pavements 综述）"],"srcs":[["Cool Pavements: State of the Art","https://www.researchgate.net/publication/360208419_Cool_Pavements_State_of_the_Art_and_New_Technologies"]],"unitEn":"℃ / kJ·kg⁻¹","titleEn":"Phase-Change Temperature and Latent Heat","descEn":"The ability of a material to absorb and release heat around its phase-change temperature with little temperature change — effectively a thermal buffer.","rangesEn":["Suitable for Shanghai summer paving; melts and absorbs heat during the day","Measured cooling occurs mainly in this window","Measured surface temperature reduction of phase-change paving","Beyond a certain dosage, further addition yields little benefit"],"targetsEn":[["Applicable context","Hard surfaces with large diurnal swing and rapid daytime heating"]],"whyEn":"It flattens the absorb-by-day, release-by-night cycle, shaving the temperature peak rather than cooling overall.","howEn":"Used in paving surface layers or mortars. Choose the phase-change point from the temperature curve of the intended hours: it must fall inside the air-temperature band you want to shave, otherwise the whole material is asleep.","watchEn":"Effective only within the phase-change band; outside it behaves as ordinary material. It releases heat at night, so pair it with night ventilation.","srcsEn":["Cool Pavements: State of the Art and New Technologies"],"casesEn":["相变铺装研究（Cool Pavements 综述）"]},"透水率与保水率":{"unit":"mm/h / %","desc":"雨水穿过铺装下渗的速率，以及材料饱和后能保住的含水量。前者管排水，后者管蒸发降温。","ranges":[["透水率 <10 mm/h","接近不透水，易积水","bad"],["10–100 mm/h","一般透水砖","warn"],[">100 mm/h","透水性能良好，可承接暴雨","ok"]],"targets":[["降噪附带收益","透水铺装可降轮胎噪声 2–8 dB"],["安全","减少行车水雾、提高抓地力"]],"why":"同一块铺装同时解决两件事：暴雨想让它透水，热浪想让它保水蒸发降温 —— 两者需要一起设计。","how":"保水型透水铺装是「被动蒸发降温」的载体：雨后储水、晴天蒸发，正是「用」雨水而非「排」雨水。适湿冷地区效果好；高湿地区效益下降（蒸发受阻），需权衡。","watch":"透水率高会降低承载力，重车通行区需另配结构；长期使用孔隙易被泥沙堵塞，需维护。","cases":["Klimaflisen 气候砖","深圳中康路海绵化"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"mm/h / %","titleEn":"Permeability and Water Retention","descEn":"The rate at which rainwater infiltrates through paving, and the water content the material retains once saturated. The first governs drainage, the second governs evaporative cooling.","rangesEn":["Close to impermeable; prone to ponding","Typical permeable brick","Good permeability; able to take cloudbursts"],"targetsEn":[["Incidental acoustic benefit","Permeable paving reduces tyre noise by 2–8 dB"],["Safety","Less spray from vehicles, better grip"]],"whyEn":"One paving surface solves two problems at once: cloudbursts want it to drain, heatwaves want it to hold water and evaporate. The two must be designed together.","howEn":"Water-retentive permeable paving is the carrier of passive evaporative cooling: it stores water after rain and evaporates it on sunny days — using rainwater rather than disposing of it. Works well in temperate humid-cold climates; benefits fall in high humidity where evaporation is restricted, so weigh the trade-off.","watchEn":"High permeability reduces load-bearing capacity; heavy-vehicle areas need a separate structure. Pores clog with silt over time and require maintenance.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Klimaflisen Climate Tile","深圳中康路海绵化"]},"被动辐射制冷涂层":{"unit":"℃","desc":"通过大气窗口（8–13 µm）把热量以长波辐射直接送入太空的涂层，无需耗能。","ranges":[["反射 97 % 太阳能","实测值","ok"],["表面温度约 −5.3 ℃","相对常规涂层的降幅","ok"],["吸水凝胶复合膜约 −7 ℃","夜间吸湿、白天蒸发，直射阳光下","ok"]],"targets":[["现阶段定位","多为原型或试点，尚未进入常规采购"]],"why":"它绕开了「降温必须耗能或耗水」的两难 —— 把热量直接辐射到外太空。","how":"适合放在最暴露、最难遮荫的面上（如无遮蔽的广场铺装、屋面、构筑物顶面）。与遮荫是互补而非替代：遮荫管「不让热进来」，辐射制冷管「让热出去」。","watch":"⚠ 仍处测试阶段，实际效果随温度、湿度与构造变化很大；涂装后可能带来眩光，需与逆反射方案配合。","cases":[],"srcs":[["被动辐射制冷技术综述（2026）","https://news.qq.com/rain/a/20260821A0CZBJ00"]],"unitEn":"℃","titleEn":"Passive Radiative Cooling Coating","descEn":"A coating that radiates heat directly to space through the atmospheric window (8–13 µm) without energy input.","rangesEn":["Measured value","Reduction relative to conventional coatings","Moisture-absorbing hydrogel composite film, night absorption and daytime evaporation, in direct sun"],"targetsEn":[["Current status","Mostly prototypes and pilots; not yet in routine procurement"]],"whyEn":"It sidesteps the dilemma that cooling must cost either energy or water — heat is radiated straight into outer space.","howEn":"Best suited to the most exposed surfaces that are hardest to shade: unshaded plaza paving, roofs, tops of structures. It complements rather than replaces shade: shade stops heat coming in, radiative cooling lets heat out.","watchEn":"Still at testing stage; performance varies greatly with temperature, humidity and construction. Coating may cause glare and should be paired with retroreflective solutions.","srcsEn":["Review of passive radiative cooling technology (2026)"],"casesEn":[]},"自修复混凝土":{"unit":"%","desc":"掺入微生物胶囊（遇水激活产生碳酸钙）或修复剂微胶囊的混凝土，裂缝出现后能自行封堵。","ranges":[["修复效率 >85 %","较早期约 60 % 已大幅提升","ok"],["结构寿命 +30~40 %","TU Delft 研究结论","ok"],["全生命周期维护成本 −50 %","研究结论","ok"]],"targets":[["适用位置","难维护、难更换的部位：基础、树池结构、地下构件"]],"why":"街道构件的寿命瓶颈常常不是设计年限，而是维护进不去、修不起。","how":"优先用在不便开挖返修的位置：树池侧壁、承台、埋地基础。对课程的意义是「把维护成本前移到材料里」——这与「谁修、谁付、怎么退」的落地三问直接对应。","watch":"成本仍高于常规混凝土，且需要长期耐久性验证；不适用于已有结构的加固。","cases":[],"srcs":[["智能材料在建筑中的应用（IEREK 2025）","https://press.ierek.com/index.php/ARChive/article/view/1243/1426"]],"unitEn":"%","titleEn":"Self-Healing Concrete","descEn":"Concrete containing microbial capsules (activated by water to produce calcium carbonate) or healing-agent microcapsules, able to seal cracks on its own.","rangesEn":["A large improvement over the roughly 60 % of earlier generations","TU Delft research conclusion","Research conclusion"],"targetsEn":[["Suitable locations","Hard-to-maintain, hard-to-replace elements: foundations, tree-pit structures, buried components"]],"whyEn":"The life-limiting factor for street components is often not the design life but the inability to get in and afford the repair.","howEn":"Prioritise positions that are costly to excavate and redo: tree-pit walls, pile caps, buried foundations. For this course the point is moving maintenance cost forward into the material — which maps directly onto the three delivery questions of who repairs, who pays, and how it is retired.","watchEn":"Still more expensive than conventional concrete and requires long-term durability verification; not applicable to strengthening existing structures.","srcsEn":["Smart materials in architecture (IEREK 2025)"],"casesEn":[]},"可移动座椅":{"unit":"把","desc":"不固定的座椅单元，使用者可自行搬动或旋转，从而改变自己的微气候与社交距离。","ranges":[["重量 8–15 kg","单人可以搬动，且不易被风掀翻","ok"],["坐面高度 400–450 mm","适老适幼的通用高度","ok"],["带扶手","起身借力，老年人使用率显著更高","ok"]],"targets":[["人均配置","每 8–12 m 街段一处可坐点"],["成效参照","悉尼 Benchmark NSW：停留时长 ×5，女性 ×8"]],"why":"固定座椅只能服从设计师给的位置；可移动座椅把「找舒服的地方」这件事交还给使用者。","how":"它是「控制权转移」最朴素、最不易失败的做法 —— 不依赖算法、不依赖供电，断电也照常工作。真正的作用是让使用者自己解决「这个时间点晒太阳还是吹风」的问题，比任何自动遮阳都灵活。","watch":"需明确管理归属，否则会被视为占道；防盗与固定方式要在不固定与不被盗之间折中。","cases":["Benchmark NSW","Street Moves","上海大学路外摆"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"pcs","titleEn":"Movable Seating","descEn":"Unfixed seating units that users can move or rotate themselves, thereby changing their own microclimate and social distance.","rangesEn":["One person can move it, and it will not blow over","Universal height suited to old and young","Significantly higher take-up among older people"],"targetsEn":[["Provision","One seatable point every 8–12 m of street"],["Evidence","Benchmark NSW, Sydney: dwell time ×5, women ×8"]],"whyEn":"Fixed seating can only obey the position the designer gave it; movable seating hands the question of finding a comfortable spot back to the user.","howEn":"It is the most plain and least failure-prone form of transferring control — no algorithm, no power supply, and it still works in a blackout. Its real function is letting users solve for themselves whether to sit in sun or wind at any given moment, which is more flexible than any automatic shading.","watchEn":"Management responsibility must be defined, otherwise it is treated as obstruction. Anti-theft and fixing must strike a balance between movable and not stolen.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Benchmark NSW","Street Moves","上海大学路外摆"]},"可开合屋面":{"unit":"m² / s","desc":"可电动展开与收拢的大型遮阳结构，按天气与时段改变遮蔽范围。","ranges":[["单伞遮荫 256–600 m²","SL Rasch 实测（侯赛因清真寺 / 麦地那）","ok"],["总遮荫 15 万 m²","麦地那圣寺广场，约 250 人 / 把伞的容量","ok"],["开合时间约 180 s","关键：太长会超出人的注意力窗口","warn"]],"targets":[["响应时长设计","180 s 需提前决策或做渐进提示"],["视线保护","主轴留空，保证从广场能看到主体建筑"]],"why":"它是「一物两用」的极致：夏天遮阳，冬天收起来让阳光进来。","how":"两种高度 + 膜面搭接，是为了让单元化产品形成连续界面 —— 这是「模块化单元如何拼出连续遮蔽」的经典答案。180 s 的开合时长提示了一个重要原则：动作时间必须落在人的注意力窗口内，否则必须给出渐进提示。","watch":"结构荷载大、造价高；收起状态需防积沙积雪与风振。","cases":["Madinah Piazza Shading","Al-Hussein Mosque"],"srcs":[["SL Rasch 项目页","https://www.sl-rasch.com/en/projects/u-26-piazza/"]],"unitEn":"m² / s","titleEn":"Deployable Canopy","descEn":"Large shading structures that deploy and retract electrically, changing their coverage with weather and time of day.","rangesEn":["SL Rasch measured values (Al-Hussein Mosque / Madinah)","Madinah Holy Mosque piazza, roughly 250 people per umbrella","Key point: any longer exceeds the human attention window"],"targetsEn":[["Response-time design","180 s requires advance decision or progressive indication"],["Sightline protection","Keep the main axis clear so the principal building stays visible from the piazza"]],"whyEn":"It is the ultimate dual-use device: shade in summer, and retracted in winter to let the sun in.","howEn":"Two heights plus membrane lapping is how a unitised product forms a continuous surface — the classic answer to how modular units tile into continuous shade. The 180 s deployment time carries an important principle: an action must fall inside the human attention window, otherwise it requires progressive indication.","watchEn":"High structural load and cost; the stowed state must resist sand and snow accumulation and wind-induced vibration.","srcsEn":["SL Rasch project page"],"casesEn":["Madinah Piazza Shading","Al-Hussein Mosque"]},"雾化降温阵列":{"unit":"℃","desc":"高压喷嘴将水打成 <10 µm 的雾滴，在空中蒸发吸热，实现局部降温。","ranges":[["RH <50 % 时","可降温 3–8 ℃","ok"],["雾化风扇","局部 5–15 ℃，影响距离约 5 m","ok"],["安装高度 2.4–3 m","效率最高的安装高度","ok"],["RH >80 % 时","基本失效，且加重闷热","bad"]],"targets":[["启用条件","RH <70 % 且有人在，才开"],["跟随式控制","端到端响应 <0.5 s（超声测距 → 阀 → 雾）"]],"why":"它是「冷却人而不是冷却空间」的代表 —— 只冷却人所在的那一米，能效可高几个数量级。","how":"三个设计要点：① 只在有人时开（否则是纯粹浪费水电）；② 必装湿度联锁，RH 超标自动停；③ 喷嘴易堵，清洗周期要写进运维表。雾区不得打湿座面与行人。","watch":"水耗与水质要管；喷嘴堵塞是最高频故障；风大时雾被吹散（>2 m/s 效果打折）。","cases":["Cloud Cast","Wiesbaden 广场喷雾","深圳光明早喷广场"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"℃","titleEn":"Misting Array","descEn":"High-pressure nozzles atomise water into droplets below 10 µm, which evaporate in the air and absorb heat, cooling locally.","rangesEn":["Cooling of 3–8 °C achievable","Local 5–15 °C, effective within about 5 m","Height with the highest efficiency","Essentially fails and worsens mugginess"],"targetsEn":[["Activation condition","Run only when RH <70 % and people are present"],["Follow-me control","End-to-end response <0.5 s (ultrasonic ranging → valve → mist)"]],"whyEn":"It represents cooling the person rather than the space — cooling only the one metre a person occupies can be orders of magnitude more efficient.","howEn":"Three design points: (1) run only when people are present, otherwise it is pure waste of water and power; (2) always fit a humidity interlock that stops above the RH threshold; (3) nozzles clog, so the cleaning cycle belongs in the maintenance schedule. The mist zone must not wet seats or pedestrians.","watchEn":"Water consumption and water quality must be managed; nozzle clogging is the most frequent fault; wind above 2 m/s disperses the mist and degrades performance.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Cloud Cast","Wiesbaden 广场喷雾","深圳光明早喷广场"]},"加热座椅":{"unit":"℃","desc":"坐面带加热的座椅，用电或回收余热把坐面维持在可坐温度。","ranges":[["坐面 30–38 ℃","冬季可坐且不烫","ok"],[">45 ℃","过烫，短裤季节不可用","bad"],["余热方案","地铁 / 车库排风经滤后导入石凳（哥本哈根实践）","ok"]],"targets":[["能耗","优先用余热而非电加热"],["冬季外摆","配合透明风挡，形成可停留的冬季微型气候"]],"why":"冬季街道的瓶颈常常不是「空气冷」，而是「坐面冰冷不敢坐」—— 加热坐面用极小的能量解决最直接的障碍。","how":"最优雅的方案是把城市已有的废热接过来：地铁与地下车库的排风常年高于室外气温，经除尘过滤后导入石材凳体，形成辐射加热。这就是「能量与资源流」这个新增大类的价值所在 —— 免费的资源一直在那里。","watch":"电加热需低压供电与漏电保护；冬季长期运行的电费要算进运维成本。","cases":["My Urban Interior（哥本哈根）"],"srcs":[["My Urban Interior","http://futurelandscapes.ca/my-urban-interior"]],"unitEn":"℃","titleEn":"Heated Seating","descEn":"Seating with a heated seat surface, using electricity or recovered waste heat to hold the seat at a sit-able temperature.","rangesEn":["Sit-able in winter without being too hot","Too hot; unusable in shorts season","Metro or garage exhaust, filtered and ducted into stone benches (Copenhagen practice)"],"targetsEn":[["Energy","Prefer waste heat over electric heating"],["Winter spill-out","Combine with transparent wind screens to form a habitable winter microclimate"]],"whyEn":"The winter bottleneck on a street is often not that the air is cold, but that the seat is too cold to dare sit on. Heating the seat surface solves the most direct obstacle with very little energy.","howEn":"The most elegant solution taps waste heat the city already has: metro and underground garage exhaust stay above outdoor air temperature year round and can be ducted, after dust filtration, into stone bench bodies to provide radiant heating. This is the value of the new energy-and-resource-flows category — free resources were there all along.","watchEn":"Electric heating requires low-voltage supply and earth-leakage protection; the winter running cost must be counted in the maintenance budget.","srcsEn":["My Urban Interior, Copenhagen"],"casesEn":["My Urban Interior（哥本哈根）"]},"花粉与致敏原":{"unit":"粒/m³","desc":"空气中致敏花粉的浓度。城市热岛与 CO₂ 升高会延长花期、增大花粉量。","ranges":[["低致敏植物","雌株（雄株产大量花粉）、无风媒花","ok"],["高致敏植物","雄株桑、豚草、栎、桦、枫","bad"],["维护干预","花前修剪与提前刈割可显著降低释放","ok"]],"targets":[["种植策略","优先雌株 + 物种多样化，避免单一树种大面积种植"]],"why":"「增加绿量」与「降低过敏」可能冲突 —— 城市历史上偏好雄株（不结果、少清扫），却恰恰是花粉大户。","how":"把致敏性列为选种条件之一：优先雌株、避免风媒花、物种多样化（避免同一花期集中爆量）、在座椅与儿童活动区周边留出缓冲带。花期与花粉预报可与维护计划挂钩。","watch":"不同人群敏感度差异极大；气味浓郁的植物对少数人也会引起不适，需控制密度。","cases":[],"srcs":[["气候驱动过敏的城市规划应对","https://climate.sustainability-directory.com/question/how-can-urban-planning-mitigate-climate-driven-allergies"]],"unitEn":"grains/m³","titleEn":"Pollen and Allergens","descEn":"Airborne allergenic pollen concentration. Urban heat islands and rising CO2 lengthen flowering seasons and increase pollen output.","rangesEn":["Female cultivars (male trees produce large amounts of pollen), non-wind-pollinated flowers","Male mulberry, ragweed, oak, birch and maple","Pre-flowering pruning and earlier mowing reduce release markedly"],"targetsEn":[["Planting strategy","Prefer female cultivars with species diversity; avoid large single-species planting"]],"whyEn":"Increasing greenery and reducing allergy can conflict. Cities have historically favoured male cultivars because they bear no fruit and need less sweeping — and those are precisely the pollen producers.","howEn":"Make allergenicity one of the selection criteria: prefer female cultivars, avoid wind-pollinated flowers, diversify species to avoid a concentrated pollen burst in one flowering window, and leave a buffer around seating and children's play areas. Flowering calendars can be linked to maintenance schedules.","watchEn":"Sensitivity varies enormously between individuals; strongly scented plants also cause discomfort for a minority, so density must be controlled.","srcsEn":["How urban planning can mitigate climate-driven allergies"],"casesEn":[]},"地下余热":{"unit":"℃","desc":"地铁、地下车库、地下商业的排风常年高于室外气温，是一种稳定存在的废热资源。","ranges":[["全年高于室外气温","冬夏季皆可用作热源或预冷","ok"],["温度稳定","不受天气波动影响，可预测","ok"]],"targets":[["利用方式","经除尘过滤后导入座椅、铺装、种植池"]],"why":"街道的能量不是只有太阳一种来源；地下空间每天都在往外排免费的温空气。","how":"识别场地内的稳定热源（地铁出口、地下车库排风口、设备机房），把它们从「影响行人的热污染」重新定义为「可用的热源」。夏季亦可用作预冷或通风驱动。这就是把排风口从问题变成资源。","watch":"空气质量必须过滤达标（含颗粒物与异味）；风量与温度需实测，不能凭估计。","cases":["My Urban Interior（哥本哈根 Metro 排风 → 辐射石凳）"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"℃","titleEn":"Underground Waste Heat","descEn":"Exhaust air from metro, underground garages and underground retail stays above outdoor air temperature year round — a stable waste-heat resource.","rangesEn":["Above outdoor temperature all year","Stable and predictable, unaffected by weather swings"],"targetsEn":[["Application","After dust filtration, duct into seating, paving or planting beds"]],"whyEn":"The sun is not the only energy source on a street. Underground spaces push free warm air out every day.","howEn":"Identify stable heat sources in the site (metro exits, garage exhaust vents, plant rooms) and redefine them from heat pollution affecting pedestrians into a usable heat source. In summer the same stream can serve pre-cooling or drive ventilation. This turns an exhaust vent from a problem into a resource.","watchEn":"Air quality must pass filtration standards (particulates and odour); flow rate and temperature need measurement, not estimation.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["My Urban Interior（哥本哈根 Metro 排风 → 辐射石凳）"]},"表面温度触感":{"unit":"℃","desc":"人直接接触的界面温度（坐面、扶手、铺装）。它决定了「敢不敢坐」这个人最直接的判断。","ranges":[["<30 ℃","可直接接触","ok"],["30–38 ℃","偏温，短时接触可接受","warn"],["38–50 ℃","长时间接触不适","warn"],[">50 ℃","不可接触（烈日下的金属与深色石材可达 60 ℃ 以上）","bad"],["<5 ℃","冰冷，冬季座位使用率骤降","warn"]],"targets":[["坐面设计目标","夏季 ≤38 ℃、冬季 ≥10 ℃"],["材质选择","木材与陶土温度波动小；金属与深色石材最不利"]],"why":"气温 35 ℃ 时，深色石材坐面可能已经 60 ℃ —— 只测气温会完全误判「能不能坐」。","how":"红外测温枪逐点巡检即可获得。材质选择比结构更有效：同样的太阳暴露下，木材表面温度显著低于石材与金属。这就是「触感与体感」必须与「材质与构造」联合看的原因。","watch":"红外读数受发射率与反射影响，抛光金属读数不可信；须固定角度重复测。","cases":["Schouwburgplein"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"℃","titleEn":"Surface Temperature and Touch","descEn":"The temperature of surfaces people touch directly — seat, handrail, paving. It decides the most immediate judgement a person makes: dare I sit here?","rangesEn":["Directly touchable","Warm; brief contact acceptable","Uncomfortable over long contact","Not touchable (metal and dark stone in sun can exceed 60 °C)","Cold; winter seat use drops sharply"],"targetsEn":[["Seat design target","≤38 °C in summer, ≥10 °C in winter"],["Material choice","Timber and terracotta fluctuate little; metal and dark stone are worst"]],"whyEn":"At an air temperature of 35 °C a dark stone seat may already be 60 °C. Measuring air temperature alone completely misjudges whether sitting is possible.","howEn":"A handheld infrared thermometer sweep delivers this. Material choice matters more than structure: under the same solar exposure, timber surfaces stay markedly cooler than stone and metal. This is why touch must be read together with material and construction.","watchEn":"Infrared readings are affected by emissivity and reflection; readings on polished metal are unreliable. Repeat from a fixed angle.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Schouwburgplein"]},"水声掩蔽":{"unit":"dB(A)","desc":"用水流声掩盖不想要的交通噪声，让听觉环境变好。掩蔽与降噪是两条不同的路。","ranges":[["掩蔽声略高于噪声源","最有效，过高反而成为新噪声","ok"],["落水 / 跌水","比平静水面掩蔽效果强得多","ok"],["吸水铺装降噪","2–8 dB（对轮胎噪声）","ok"]],"targets":[["布置位置","靠近噪声源而不是靠近休息区 —— 在人耳与噪声之间"]],"why":"降 5 dB 的噪声要付很高代价，而引入一个愉悦声源几乎不费什么钱，效果却更可感。","how":"把水声当成「声学构件」来设计：选跌水而非静水、控制掩蔽声级略高于交通噪声、位置放在人耳与噪声源之间。与视觉上的「水的可见性」配合，同时作用两个感官。","watch":"夜间与冬季水声可能扰民或结冰；水景维护（藻类、落叶、水泵）是长期负担。","cases":["Sheffield 车站前庭水景"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"dB(A)","titleEn":"Water Sound Masking","descEn":"Covering unwanted traffic noise with the sound of flowing water to improve the acoustic environment. Masking and noise reduction are two different routes.","rangesEn":["Most effective; too loud and it becomes a new noise source","Falling or dropping water masks far better than still water","Against tyre noise"],"targetsEn":[["Position","Near the noise source, not near the resting area — between the ear and the noise"]],"whyEn":"Cutting noise by 5 dB is expensive; adding a pleasant sound source costs almost nothing and is more immediately perceptible.","howEn":"Design water sound as an acoustic component: choose falling water over still water, set the masking level slightly above the traffic noise, and place it between the ear and the source. Pair it with the visibility of water so two senses are engaged at once.","watchEn":"Water sound can disturb neighbours at night or freeze in winter; water feature maintenance (algae, leaves, pumps) is a long-term burden.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Sheffield 车站前庭水景"]},"眩光规避":{"unit":"—","desc":"避免过强或过亮的直射光、反射光进入视野造成视觉不适与短暂失能。","ranges":[["高反射铺装的反射眩光","与「提高反照率降温」直接冲突","bad"],["夜间溢光","影响周边居住与天空可见度","warn"],["低角度太阳直射","清晨与傍晚，东西向街道最严重","warn"]],"targets":[["材料对策","用逆反射材料（把光垂直反射回天）替代镜面反射"],["布局对策","在东西向街道的西侧优先布置遮荫与绿篱"]],"why":"它是「降温做得越好、眩光可能越严重」的典型冲突项 —— 冷铺装与眩光往往同时出现。","how":"先把眩光当成冷铺装的前置条件而不是副作用：选逆反射而非镜面反射材料，或在可能产生眩光的开敞段改为「用遮荫降温」而不靠提高反射率。夜间则控制灯具的溢光与被照面亮度比。","watch":"眩光评价带主观性，宜结合现场实测与问卷，不能只算指标。","cases":[],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"—","titleEn":"Glare Avoidance","descEn":"Avoiding excessively strong or bright direct and reflected light entering the field of view, causing visual discomfort and momentary disability.","rangesEn":["Directly conflicts with raising albedo for cooling","Affects nearby residents and sky visibility","Most severe on east-west streets"],"targetsEn":[["Material response","Use retroreflective materials (returning light vertically to the sky) instead of specular reflection"],["Layout response","Prioritise shade and hedges on the western side of east-west streets"]],"whyEn":"This is the archetypal conflict where doing the cooling well can make glare worse — cool pavements and glare often arrive together.","howEn":"Treat glare as a precondition for cool paving rather than a side effect: choose retroreflective rather than specular materials, or in open segments where glare is likely, cool by shade instead of by reflectance. At night, control spill light and the luminance ratio of lit surfaces.","watchEn":"Glare assessment is subjective; combine field measurement with questionnaires rather than relying on an index alone.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":[]},"异位愉悦 alliesthesia":{"unit":"—","desc":"人对同一刺激的愉悦程度取决于当时的内环境状态：在不适状态下，微小的环境改善会带来远超比例的愉悦感。","ranges":[["不适状态下的微小改变","立即生效且效果显著（数分钟内可测）","ok"],["已舒适状态下的同等改变","几乎不被感知","info"]],"targets":[["设计含义","把资源投在「最不舒服的那一刻、那一个点」"]],"why":"这是本项目最重要的一条理论支撑 —— 它解释了为什么小干预也能有大效果，而不必追求整体降温。","how":"三条可操作结论：① 不必整体降温，只需在峰值时段的局部给人一点缓解；② 干预要落在「刚出现不适」的时点与位置（如西晒的那半米、午后 14–16 时）；③ 多个感官的小改善会叠加（一小簇香气 + 一片荫 + 一点风），比单一感官的大改善更容易被感知。","watch":"个体差异大；过敏与感官敏感人群对气味、光的容忍度低，需留出可回避的空间。","cases":["Cloud Cast（人走过才喷雾）","Wiesbaden 喷雾（触摸即启、3 分钟自停）"],"srcs":[["多感官恢复性效益系统综述（Land 2024）","https://www.mdpi.com/2073-445X/13/12/2018"]],"unitEn":"—","titleEn":"Alliesthesia","descEn":"The pleasantness of the same stimulus depends on the body's internal state: in discomfort, a small environmental improvement produces pleasure far out of proportion to its size.","rangesEn":["Takes effect within minutes and is easy to measure","Barely perceived at equivalent magnitude in an already comfortable state"],"targetsEn":[["Design implication","Spend resources on the least comfortable moment and point"]],"whyEn":"This is the most important theoretical support for the project — it explains why a small intervention can have a large effect without pursuing overall cooling.","howEn":"Three operational conclusions: (1) no need to cool everything, only to relieve the local point during peak hours; (2) place the intervention where discomfort first appears, such as the west-facing half metre or 14:00–16:00; (3) small improvements across several senses add up — a little scent, a patch of shade and a breath of air are more perceptible than one large single-sense improvement.","watchEn":"Individual variation is large; people with allergies and sensory sensitivity tolerate odour and light poorly and need somewhere to withdraw to.","srcsEn":["Systematic review of multisensory restorative benefits (Land 2024)"],"casesEn":["Cloud Cast（人走过才喷雾）","Wiesbaden 喷雾（触摸即启、3 分钟自停）"]},"热应激风险分级":{"unit":"℃","desc":"按人体热负荷把环境分成可操作的风险等级，用于决定「什么时段、什么人群可以待在户外」。","ranges":[["UTCI 9–26 ℃","无热应激","ok"],["26–32 ℃","中等热应激","warn"],["32–38 ℃","强热应激","bad"],[">38 ℃","极强热应激，应避免户外停留","bad"],["<9 ℃","冷应激出现","warn"],["亚热带冬季参考","UTCI 20–22 ℃ 可作舒适设计目标","info"]],"targets":[["人群差异化","老年人的中性温度更高，需更暖的微环境"],["对应要求","为高龄使用者提供比常规再暖 2–3 ℃ 的微空间"]],"why":"同一个环境对不同人群的风险完全不同 —— 把「人是谁」写进环境判断，才能定出真实的可用时段。","how":"用分级而不是平均值来指导设计：为每个等级定出「可停留时长」与「需要的干预」，再据此配置遮荫、座椅与提示。分级还能直接支撑汇报叙事 —— 「这个设计把 38 ℃ 以上的不可用时段减少了 N 小时」。","watch":"分级阈值需本地化标定：上海夏热冬冷，不能直接套用热带或北欧的中性温度。","cases":["Seeing the Heat（米兰 PET 分级）"],"srcs":[["沈阳 Dwa 气候区中性 PET 阈值研究（2026）","https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-026-46003-0"],["香港冬季热舒适基准（CUHK）","https://research.cuhk.edu.hk/en/publications/designing-for-mild-winters-evidence-based-thermal-comfort-benchma"]],"unitEn":"℃","titleEn":"Heat Stress Risk Bands","descEn":"Classifying the environment by human heat load into actionable risk levels, used to decide who can be outdoors at which hours.","rangesEn":["No heat stress","Moderate heat stress","Strong heat stress","Very strong heat stress; avoid outdoor exposure","Cold stress appears","Sub-tropical winter reference, usable as a comfortable design target"],"targetsEn":[["Population differentiation","Older adults have a higher neutral temperature and need warmer microclimates"],["Corresponding requirement","Provide micro-spaces 2–3 °C warmer than conventional for older users"]],"whyEn":"The same environment carries completely different risk for different people. Writing who the user is into the environmental judgement is what makes real usable hours definable.","howEn":"Use bands rather than averages: define usable duration and required interventions for each band, then configure shade, seating and signage accordingly. Bands also support the narrative — this design cut the unusable hours above 38 °C by N hours.","watchEn":"Thresholds must be locally calibrated: Shanghai is hot in summer and cold in winter, so tropical or Nordic neutral temperatures cannot be applied directly.","srcsEn":["Study of neutral PET thresholds in the Dwa climate zone, Shenyang (2026)","Designing for mild winters: evidence-based thermal comfort benchmarks (CUHK)"],"casesEn":["Seeing the Heat（米兰 PET 分级）"]},"植物芳香":{"unit":"—","desc":"植物挥发性有机物（BVOC）随风扩散形成的嗅觉环境。浓度随温度、湿度与时段剧烈变化，不是一个恒定值。","ranges":[["气温 25–30 ℃","多数芳香植物释放量最高","ok"],["气温 >35 ℃","气孔关闭，释放量骤降 —— 越热反而越闻不到","warn"],["RH >85 %","气味分子被水汽包裹，扩散与辨识都变差","warn"],["距源 1–3 m（无风时更近）","可稳定辨识的区间","ok"],["距源 >8 m","多数香气难以稳定辨识","info"]],"targets":[["种植单元间距","沿步行路径每 15–25 m 设一处气味点"],["气味高度","控制在 0.8–1.8 m（坐姿与站姿的呼吸带）"]],"why":"气味与记忆、情绪绑定最紧，却最难被「看见」。而人对气味的适应极快 —— 进入有香环境几分钟后便不再察觉，所以「香」必须靠位置变化来维持，不能靠浓度堆叠。","how":"三条可操作规则：① 「不要混种」—— 不同香气叠加会互相抵消，人只感到「乱香」；② 气味要有「口袋」—— 沿路径间隔布置，让人一走一过反复「重新闻到」；③ 高度决定体验 —— 把芳香植物抬到 0.8–1.8 m 的呼吸带（花池台面、立体花架），比种在地面有效得多。选种优先本地耐候品种，并让花期错开。","watch":"过敏与气味敏感人群（尤其哮喘、偏头痛患者）对浓香容忍度极低；不宜紧贴座椅与儿童活动区，应留出可回避的路径。高温高湿时香气易显「闷」。","cases":["广州花都香水花园","广州旧南海县社区香景改造","上海「脑迷宫」花园"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"—","titleEn":"Plant Fragrance","descEn":"The olfactory environment created by biogenic volatile organic compounds (BVOCs) dispersing on the wind. Concentration varies sharply with temperature, humidity and time of day — it is never a constant.","rangesEn":["Peak release for most aromatic species","Stomata close and release drops sharply — the hotter it gets, the less you smell","Scent molecules are wrapped in water vapour; both dispersion and recognition suffer","The band where scent can be reliably identified","Most scents become hard to identify reliably"],"targetsEn":[["Planting unit spacing","One scent point every 15–25 m along a walking route"],["Scent height","Keep within 0.8–1.8 m, the breathing zone when seated and standing"]],"whyEn":"Smell is bound most tightly to memory and emotion, yet is the hardest sense to design visibly. And adaptation is fast — within minutes in a scented environment you stop noticing. Scent must therefore be sustained by change of position, not by stacking concentration.","howEn":"Three operational rules. (1) Do not mix species: layered scents cancel each other and the visitor registers only confusion. (2) Give scent pockets: place them at intervals along the route so that walking past re-triggers perception. (3) Height decides experience: raising aromatic planting into the 0.8–1.8 m breathing zone (raised planters, tiered stands) is far more effective than planting at ground level. Prefer site-adapted local species and stagger flowering periods.","watchEn":"People with allergies and scent sensitivity — asthma and migraine sufferers especially — tolerate strong scent very poorly. Do not plant aromatic species hard against seats and children's play areas; leave a route to withdraw. In hot humid weather scent reads as stuffy.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["广州花都香水花园","广州旧南海县社区香景改造","上海「脑迷宫」花园"]},"负面气味规避":{"unit":"—","desc":"对垃圾点、空调外机、餐饮排烟、雨污水井等气味源的识别、隔离与遮蔽。气味设计有一半是「去掉坏味」，而这一半常被跳过。","ranges":[["距气味源 <5 m","明显感知（夏季下风向更差）","bad"],["距气味源 5–15 m","可感知但不主导","warn"],["距气味源 >15 m","一般不构成干扰","ok"],["下风向 10 m ≈ 上风向 5 m","风向比距离更重要","info"]],"targets":[["布点原则","先切断扩散路径，再考虑掩蔽"],["隔离方式","绿篱 / 构筑遮挡；排风口导向上部"]],"why":"负面气味对停留意愿的破坏远大于正面香气带来的提升 —— 一处垃圾点足以让整段街道没人愿意坐下。这是短板效应最明显的感官维度。","how":"按「避 — 隔 — 掩」三级处理：① 避 —— 布点前先查风玫瑰，把停留区放在气味源的上风向；② 隔 —— 用绿篱或实体挡墙切断传播，同时把排风口导向上部；③ 掩 —— 前两级做完再谈芳香掩蔽。街道上最常见的失手是把座椅正对空调外机或餐饮排烟口 —— 测气温完全正常，但没人愿意坐。","watch":"掩蔽是补救而不是解决方案；对垃圾点这类持续性负源，掩蔽只会变成「香臭混合」，感知反而更糟。","cases":["谢菲尔德 Parkwood Springs 气味景观再生"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"—","titleEn":"Avoiding Negative Odours","descEn":"Identifying, isolating and screening odour sources such as bin stores, air-conditioner units, kitchen exhaust and drainage gullies. Half of scent design is removing the bad smells, and that half is usually skipped.","rangesEn":["Clearly perceptible, worse downwind in summer","Perceptible but not dominant","Generally not disruptive","Wind direction matters more than distance"],"targetsEn":[["Siting principle","Cut the dispersal path before considering masking"],["Isolation method","Hedges or solid screens; duct exhaust outlets upwards"]],"whyEn":"Negative odour damages the willingness to stay far more than positive scent improves it. A single bin store is enough to empty a whole stretch of seats. This is the sensory dimension where the weakest-link effect is most obvious.","howEn":"Handle in three tiers: avoid, isolate, mask. First check the wind rose before siting and put seating upwind of odour sources. Then cut dispersal with hedges or solid screens and duct exhausts upwards. Only then consider aromatic masking. The commonest failure on real streets is seating placed facing an air-conditioner unit or kitchen exhaust — air temperature measures perfectly normal, yet nobody will sit there.","watchEn":"Masking is a remedy, not a solution. Against continuous sources like bin stores it merely produces a mixture of perfume and rot, which reads worse.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["谢菲尔德 Parkwood Springs 气味景观再生"]},"气味口袋与路径化布置":{"unit":"m","desc":"把芳香植物按间隔布置成一个个「气味斑块」，沿步行路径串联，用位置变化对抗嗅觉适应。","ranges":[["口袋间距 15–25 m","按步行速度约 10–20 s 一次，短于嗅觉适应时间","ok"],["口袋间距 >40 m","中间段气味断层，体验断裂","warn"],["单个口袋面积 1–4 m²","足以被感知，不必成片","ok"]],"targets":[["密度","一条 200 m 街段设 8–12 个气味口袋"],["与停留点关系","座椅与候车点位于口袋的上风侧 1–3 m"]],"why":"人对气味的适应在几分钟内完成 —— 浓度再高，站在原地也不会一直闻到。所以气味不能靠「一整片花海」，而要靠「反复路过」。这与视觉体验的逻辑正好相反。","how":"沿路径做等间隔的气味口袋，每个口袋选一种主调（薄荷 / 迷迭香 / 柑橘 / 桂花），相邻口袋不用同一香气，让人在行走中获得「序列」。这实质是把听觉里的「声景层次」翻译成嗅觉的做法。口袋可以就是普通花池，不必增加构件成本 —— 差别只在间距与植物高度的控制。","watch":"口袋不宜设在风口，否则气味被吹散、感知不到；也不宜设在完全静风的死角，气味会积成「闷味」。","cases":["广州花都香水花园","谢菲尔德 Parkwood Springs 气味景观再生"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"m","titleEn":"Scent Pockets along Routes","descEn":"Placing aromatic planting as a series of discrete scent patches strung along a walking route, using change of position to counter olfactory adaptation.","rangesEn":["About 10–20 s apart at walking speed, shorter than the adaptation time","A scent gap opens in between and the experience breaks","Enough to be perceived; no need for a continuous bed"],"targetsEn":[["Density","8–12 scent pockets along a 200 m street segment"],["Relation to resting points","Seats and waiting points sit 1–3 m upwind of a pocket"]],"whyEn":"Olfactory adaptation completes within minutes — however high the concentration, standing still in one spot you stop smelling it. Scent therefore cannot rely on a single 'sea of flowers' but on repeated passing. This is the exact opposite of how visual experience works.","howEn":"Place evenly spaced pockets along the route, each with one dominant note (mint, rosemary, citrus, osmanthus), and never repeat the same note in adjacent pockets, so that walking produces a sequence. This is effectively translating acoustic layering into smell. A pocket can simply be an ordinary planter — no extra component cost, only control of spacing and plant height.","watchEn":"Avoid windy spots, where scent is dispersed below perception, and avoid dead-still corners, where it accumulates into stuffiness.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["广州花都香水花园","谢菲尔德 Parkwood Springs 气味景观再生"]},"雨后土气与湿润感":{"unit":"—","desc":"降雨后土壤与铺装散发的清新气息（主要成分为土臭素 geosmin 与植物释放的油脂），是跨文化评价最高的自然气味之一。","ranges":[["雨后 0–2 h","土臭素浓度峰值，气味最鲜明","ok"],["雨后 2–6 h","残留湿感，气味转淡","ok"],["透水铺装 + 种植床","雨后气味持续时间显著长于硬质铺装","ok"],["过度密封的铺装","几乎无雨后气味，只留积水","warn"]],"targets":[["材料选择","保留可吸水、可散发的地面（透水铺装、裸土、树池）"],["与降温协同","保水铺装雨后蒸发降温与此同源，一次投入两重收益"]],"why":"这是成本最低、接受度最高的嗅觉体验 —— 不需要种任何芳香植物，只需要地面能吸水。而且它与蒸发降温在物理上是同一件事。","how":"把「蒸发降温」与「嗅觉体验」合并处理：保水型透水铺装雨时储水、晴时蒸发，既降低表面温度，又延长雨后气味。要避免的做法是全硬化 + 快速排干 —— 街道虽然不积水，但也就失去了这一层体验。与海绵化措施是同一件事的两个收益。","watch":"高湿地区（如上海梅雨期）土壤长期饱和时，气味会从「清新」转向「闷霉」，必须保证排水与换气。","cases":["Klimaflisen 气候砖","中康路海绵化改造"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"—","titleEn":"Petrichor and Post-Rain Dampness","descEn":"The fresh smell released by soil and paving after rain — mainly geosmin and plant oils — one of the most universally liked natural scents across cultures.","rangesEn":["Peak geosmin concentration; the smell is at its most vivid","Residual dampness; scent fades","Scent persists markedly longer than on hard paving","Almost no post-rain scent; only standing water remains"],"targetsEn":[["Material choice","Keep ground that can absorb and release water: permeable paving, bare soil, tree pits"],["Synergy with cooling","Water-retentive paving cools by evaporation after rain — the same act, two benefits"]],"whyEn":"This is the cheapest and most widely accepted olfactory experience. It requires no aromatic planting at all — only ground that can absorb water. And physically it is the same phenomenon as evaporative cooling.","howEn":"Handle evaporative cooling and olfactory experience as one problem: water-retentive permeable paving stores rain and evaporates it on fine days, lowering surface temperature and extending the post-rain scent. What to avoid is full hard surfacing plus rapid drainage — the street no longer ponds, but this layer of experience disappears with the water. Sponge-city measures give both benefits from one investment.","watchEn":"In humid regions such as the Shanghai plum-rain season, long-saturated soil turns the smell from fresh to musty; drainage and air exchange are essential.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Klimaflisen Climate Tile","Zhongkang Road Sponge City Retrofit"]},"高湿闷味与霉味":{"unit":"%","desc":"长期高湿下有机质（落叶、土壤、积水盘）腐败产生的霉味与闷味，是梅雨地区最常见的负面嗅觉体验。","ranges":[["RH >80 % 持续 >3 天","霉味开始出现","warn"],["RH >85 % 且气温 >28 ℃","闷味与霉味叠加，体感显著恶化","bad"],["积水停滞 >48 h","厌氧发酵，气味急剧恶化","bad"],["有遮荫 + 良好通风","地表温湿度下降，霉味明显减轻","ok"]],"targets":[["上海梅雨期","以通风、排水与可拆卸构造替代密闭湿区"],["落叶管理","树下铺装避免形成积水盘，落叶清运周期 ≤3 天"]],"why":"上海夏热冬冷、梅雨期长，湿热是最真实的本地胁迫组合 —— 而「闷味」正是把热、湿两个胁迫因子叠加成的嗅觉体验，在气候响应设计里常被完全忽略。","how":"三条对策：① 「不给水停留的机会」—— 树下与花池做不积水构造、落叶及时清运，因为厌氧发酵的前提是有机质长期泡水；② 「用通风换气」—— 遮荫与通风要同时做，避免形成又阴又湿又不动的死角；③ 「材质上避免长期吸水的多孔有机材料」（未处理木材、密实草皮）在长期潮湿区使用。这与「适湿地区慎用蒸发降温」是同一条物理逻辑。","watch":"霉味常与霉菌孢子同时出现，对呼吸道敏感人群影响更大 —— 不能只按「好不好闻」判断，需纳入健康指标。","cases":[],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"%","titleEn":"Mustiness under High Humidity","descEn":"The musty, stuffy smell produced when organic matter — fallen leaves, soil, water-retaining trays — decomposes under prolonged high humidity. The commonest negative olfactory experience in plum-rain regions.","rangesEn":["Mustiness begins to appear","Stuffy and musty smell compound; felt conditions deteriorate sharply","Anaerobic fermentation; smell degrades rapidly","Surface temperature and humidity fall; mustiness markedly reduced"],"targetsEn":[["Shanghai plum-rain season","Use ventilation, drainage and demountable construction instead of sealed damp zones"],["Leaf management","Avoid water-retaining trays under trees; clear fallen leaves within 3 days"]],"whyEn":"Shanghai is hot in summer and cold in winter with a long plum-rain season, and hot-humid is the most real local stressor combination. Stuffy smell is exactly what heat and humidity combine into in olfactory terms — and it is almost entirely absent from climate-responsive design.","howEn":"Three responses. (1) Give water no chance to stand: build tree pits and planters so they do not retain water, and clear leaves promptly, since anaerobic fermentation requires organic matter to sit in water. (2) Ventilate: shade and ventilation must be designed together, avoiding dead corners that are simultaneously shaded, damp and still. (3) Avoid porous organic materials that stay wet long term (untreated timber, dense turf) in permanently damp zones. This is the same physical logic as being cautious with evaporative cooling in humid climates.","watchEn":"Mustiness usually accompanies mould spores, which affect people with respiratory sensitivity more severely. Do not judge on pleasantness alone; treat it as a health indicator.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":[]},"文化气味与集体记忆":{"unit":"—","desc":"特定气味与地方文化绑定形成的认同感，如桂花之于江南、咖啡之于街角、面包之于清晨。","ranges":[["与在地物候绑定","桂花（秋）、蜡梅（冬）等季节性气味辨识度最高","ok"],["与日常商业绑定","咖啡、面包等气味出现频次高、可稳定预期","ok"],["与节庆绑定","年节食物气味承载集体记忆","ok"],["脱离本地经验的气味","对游客可能不成立，辨识度低","info"]],"targets":[["设计策略","每季至少一种可辨识的在香气味，形成年度节奏"],["与导视结合","气味可承担定位功能 —— 闻香识路"]],"why":"气味是唯一直接连到记忆中枢的感官，因此也是建立场所认同最快的通道 —— 人说不清为什么喜欢一条街，往往是因为某个气味。","how":"把气味写进季节日历：春季柑橘花、夏季薄荷与栀子、秋季桂花、冬季蜡梅，让同一条街在一年里有四次「可期待的气味事件」（与 E7 时间与事件性直接联动）。商业气味（B6.2 食物气味与商业）是另一条低成本路径 —— 咖啡与烘焙气味几乎无需维护，只要允许这类业态存在。","watch":"文化气味的辨识度依赖本地生活经验，对游客可能不成立；不要把它当作唯一线索。","cases":["广州旧南海县社区香景改造","上海「脑迷宫」花园"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"—","titleEn":"Cultural Scent and Collective Memory","descEn":"Feelings of identity produced when particular smells are bound to local culture — osmanthus in Jiangnan, coffee on a street corner, bread in the early morning.","rangesEn":["Seasonal scents such as osmanthus (autumn) and wintersweet (winter) are the most recognisable","Coffee and bread appear frequently and can be reliably expected","Festival food smells carry collective memory","Scents outside local experience may not register for visitors"],"targetsEn":[["Design strategy","At least one recognisable in-place scent per season, forming an annual rhythm"],["Link with wayfinding","Scent can carry a locating function — find the way by smell"]],"whyEn":"Smell is the only sense wired directly into the memory centres, which makes it the fastest route to place identity. People often cannot say why they like a street — frequently it is a smell.","howEn":"Write scent into a seasonal calendar: citrus blossom in spring, mint and gardenia in summer, osmanthus in autumn, wintersweet in winter — four anticipated smell events a year on the same street, directly linked to temporality and eventfulness. Commercial scent (food aroma and retail) is the other low-cost route: coffee and bakery smells need almost no maintenance, only the permission for those businesses to exist.","watchEn":"Recognition of cultural scent depends on lived local experience and may not hold for visitors. Do not make it the only cue.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["广州旧南海县社区香景改造","上海「脑迷宫」花园"]},"风过叶片与雨打顶棚":{"unit":"dB(A)","desc":"由植物、构筑与雨水相互作用产生的自然声，是声景里接受度最高的声源类型。","ranges":[["阔叶树（杨、梧桐等）","风声层次丰富，宽频、无音调","ok"],["针叶与禾本科","高频细碎声，适合近距离","ok"],["雨打张拉膜 / 金属屋面 60–75 dB(A)","雨声被放大，可掩蔽交通噪声，但需控制对室内的干扰","ok"],["雨打硬质顶棚 >80 dB(A)","交谈受阻，必须做吸声处理","warn"]],"targets":[["构件设计","顶棚做微起伏或加吸声层，把雨声调成悦耳声源而不是噪声"],["与排水结合","檐口做法同时决定声与水的路径"]],"why":"这是把气候现象直接变成体验的最短路径 —— 同一场雨，落在硬质顶棚上是负担，落在合适构造上是资源。它不需要新增设备，只需要在选材料、定构造时多想一步。","how":"三类做法：① 用阔叶树冠制造风声（选叶柄细长的树种，风起即有声）；② 张拉膜或轻钢顶棚刻意利用雨声掩蔽交通噪声，但要做吸声与坡度设计，避免积水与过响；③ 在檐口与水链处引导雨水形成可控的跌水声（与 B5.1 水声掩蔽同源）。本质是把「隔声」思路换成「利用声」，代价通常远低于降噪。","watch":"需与室内声环境协调（沿街商铺顶棚雨声过大影响经营）；夜间水声与雨声可能扰民；冬季结冰会改变甚至消除声效。","cases":["Plaza GLT 声景更新","上海「心巢·归源」生态疗愈花园"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"dB(A)","titleEn":"Wind in Leaves, Rain on Canopies","descEn":"Natural sound produced by plants, structures and rainwater interacting — the most accepted class of sound source in a soundscape.","rangesEn":["Rich, broadband, non-tonal wind sound","Fine high-frequency sound, suited to close range","Rain sound amplified; can mask traffic noise but interior impact must be controlled","Conversation obstructed; acoustic absorption required"],"targetsEn":[["Component design","Give canopies slight undulation or add an absorptive layer so rain reads as a pleasant source rather than noise"],["Combined with drainage","Eaves detail determines both the path of sound and the path of water"]],"whyEn":"This is the shortest route from climate phenomenon to experience. The same rain is a burden on a hard canopy and a resource on a well-considered one. It needs no new equipment — only one extra thought when choosing materials and details.","howEn":"Three approaches. (1) Use broadleaf canopies to generate wind sound; species with slender petioles sound as soon as wind rises. (2) Tensile membrane or light steel canopies can deliberately use rain sound to mask traffic noise, but need absorption and slope design to avoid ponding and excessive level. (3) Guide rainwater at eaves and chain downpipes to form controlled falling-water sound, the same family as water sound masking. The essence is swapping sound insulation for sound use, usually far cheaper than noise reduction.","watchEn":"Must be coordinated with interior acoustics — excessive rain sound on shopfront canopies harms trade. Night-time water and rain sound can disturb residents. Ice in winter changes or removes the effect entirely.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Plaza GLT 声景更新","上海「心巢·归源」生态疗愈花园"]},"安静区与自然声":{"unit":"dB(A)","desc":"在街区中划出低声级、以自然声主导的停留区域，作为高噪声环境里的听觉庇护所。","ranges":[["<55 dB(A)","可称为安静区（居住区夜间参考值）","ok"],["55–60 dB(A)","自然声可辨识、交谈轻松","ok"],["60–65 dB(A)","自然声偶尔可辨，需提高音量交谈","warn"],[">65 dB(A)","自然声被完全掩盖，停留意愿显著下降","bad"],["自然声与噪声差 <3 dB","自然声难以被识别 —— 看信噪比而不是绝对声级","bad"]],"targets":[["安静区进深","至少 8–10 m，且与车行道之间有屏障"],["自然声可辨时间占比","目标 ≥40 %"]],"why":"声景设计的目标不是「更安静」，而是「能听出层次」。自然声对压力的恢复效益显著，但前提是它必须能被听到 —— 在 70 dB(A) 的干道旁种一片竹林几乎没有意义。","how":"先用声级计找出街段中自然形成的「洼地」（通常是被建筑或绿篱遮挡的转角），把它定义为安静区并优先配置座椅；再用屏障把交通噪声再压 5–10 dB，抬升自然声的相对占比。关键判据是信噪比而不是绝对声级 —— 掩蔽声或自然声只要不低于噪声源 3 dB 就能被感知（见「水声掩蔽」）。这与「在城市里找个安静的角」的直觉一致，只是给出了量化门槛。","watch":"安静区需要「防打扰」—— 必须把外卖车、空调外机、垃圾清运点排在区外，否则安静区会被自己的配套毁掉。","cases":["南京玄武湖无障碍花园","Plaza GLT 声景更新"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"dB(A)","titleEn":"Quiet Zones and Natural Sound","descEn":"Quiet, nature-sound-dominated resting zones carved out of a street, serving as acoustic refuges within a noisy environment.","rangesEn":["Qualifies as a quiet area (residential night-time reference)","Natural sound identifiable; conversation easy","Natural sound occasionally identifiable; raised voice needed","Natural sound fully masked; willingness to stay drops sharply","Natural sound is hard to identify — read signal-to-noise ratio, not absolute level"],"targetsEn":[["Depth of quiet zone","At least 8–10 m, with a barrier between it and the carriageway"],["Share of time natural sound is discernible","Target ≥40 %"]],"whyEn":"The goal of soundscape design is not to be quieter but to remain legible. Natural sound has measurable restorative benefit, but only if it can actually be heard — planting a bamboo grove beside a 70 dB(A) arterial road achieves almost nothing.","howEn":"Use a sound level meter to find the dips the street already forms, usually corners screened by buildings or hedges, designate them as quiet zones and give them seats first. Then use barriers to press traffic noise down another 5–10 dB so the relative share of natural sound rises. The key criterion is signal-to-noise ratio rather than absolute level: a masker or natural sound is perceptible as long as it is not more than 3 dB below the noise source (see water sound masking). This matches the instinct of finding a quiet corner in the city, but gives it a quantitative threshold.","watchEn":"Quiet zones need protection from their own supporting uses — keep delivery scooters, air-conditioner units and refuse collections outside, or the zone is destroyed by its own amenities.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["南京玄武湖无障碍花园","Plaza GLT 声景更新"]},"声源方位感":{"unit":"°","desc":"声源与噪声源在空间上分开时，人对掩蔽效果的感知差异。这是决定水景放在哪里、有没有用的关键参数。","ranges":[["分离角 <135°","掩蔽有效（水景落在使用者视野内）","ok"],["分离角 135°","感知响度约增加 1–2 dB，效果明显下降","warn"],["分离角 180°","整体声景质量下降，等效于噪声提高 2–5 dB","bad"],["人正常视野 <135°","因此水景必须布置在视野范围内才成立","info"]],"targets":[["布置原则","水景放在人耳与噪声源之间，且在使用者的视野内"],["要避免","把水景放在人背后或视野之外"]],"why":"这一条推翻了「水景放在哪都能降噪」的直觉 —— 视觉与听觉是耦合的。实验证据表明，当水声与噪声源在方位上分开超过 135°（也就是水景落在视野之外），掩蔽的心理效益会大幅衰减，甚至比不放水景更差。","how":"落地只有一句话：「让使用者同时看到水和听到水，且水在他与噪声源之间」。设计动作是：先确定停留区的朝向与人眼视野扇形，再确定噪声源方位，把水景放在两者的连线上。这也解释了为什么「背对马路的水景座椅」通常体验不佳。","watch":"该结论来自虚拟现实听音实验，现场条件下建筑反射与风会改变结果，宜现场复核。","cases":["Plaza GLT 声景更新","蒙特利尔三版雾森广场"],"srcs":[["The effects of spatial separations between water sound and traffic noise sources on soundscape assessment (Building and Environment)","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S036013231930633X"]],"unitEn":"°","titleEn":"Sound Source Bearing","descEn":"How perceived masking effectiveness changes when the sound source and the noise source are separated in space. This is the parameter that decides whether a water feature works and where it should go.","rangesEn":["Masking effective — the water feature falls within the user's field of view","Perceived loudness rises by roughly 1–2 dB; effectiveness falls markedly","Overall soundscape quality drops, equivalent to a 2–5 dB rise in noise","So a water feature must be placed within the field of view to work at all"],"targetsEn":[["Placement principle","Water between the ear and the noise source, and within the user's field of view"],["What to avoid","Putting the water feature behind the user or outside the field of view"]],"whyEn":"This overturns the instinct that a water feature reduces noise wherever it is placed — vision and hearing are coupled. Experimental evidence shows that when water sound and traffic noise are separated by more than 135°, that is when the feature falls outside the field of view, the psychological benefit of masking decays badly and can end up worse than no feature at all.","howEn":"It comes down to one sentence: let the user see the water and hear the water at the same time, with the water between them and the noise source. In design terms, first fix the orientation of the seating area and the human visual cone, then fix the noise source bearing, then put the feature on the line between them. This also explains why water features with seats facing away from the road usually feel poor.","watchEn":"The finding comes from a virtual-reality listening experiment; on site, building reflections and wind change the outcome, so verify in place.","srcsEn":["The effects of spatial separations between water sound and traffic noise sources on soundscape assessment (Building and Environment)"],"casesEn":["Plaza GLT 声景更新","Montreal Three Misters Square"]},"声景层次与私密性":{"unit":"—","desc":"同一空间里多种声源（人声、水声、风声、远处交通）的可分辨程度，决定交谈的私密感与空间的「厚度」。","ranges":[["人声可辨且不被掩盖","交谈舒适，私密性良好","ok"],["连续稳态噪声主导","人声需提高音量，疲劳感增加","warn"],["混响过长或声源过密","交谈困难、无法私密","warn"],["有连续低声级掩蔽源（水、风）","交谈私密性提升","ok"]],"targets":[["座位布置","背靠实体（绿篱、墙体）比背对开敞空间更私密"],["掩蔽策略","用连续低声级声源把连续座位切成小声学单元"]],"why":"街道声景不是「越安静越好」—— 餐饮外摆真正需要的是「交谈不被旁人听清」的私密性，而这一点恰好可以靠引入连续水流声实现。这与降噪是完全不同的目标。","how":"把声景当成空间分区工具：用连续水声或树冠风声形成「声幕」，把连续排布的座位切分成若干小声学单元，每个单元内的交谈不会被邻座干扰 —— 这是咖啡馆声学在街道上的翻版。座位布局上，背靠实体的一侧天然更私密。","watch":"掩蔽声级过高会反过来影响交谈（信噪比失衡），需实测调校。","cases":["Plaza GLT 声景更新"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"—","titleEn":"Soundscape Layers and Privacy","descEn":"The degree to which multiple sound sources in one space — voices, water, wind, distant traffic — can be told apart. It determines conversational privacy and the thickness of a space.","rangesEn":["Speech audible and unmasked; comfortable conversation, good privacy","Continuous steady noise dominates; raised voice and fatigue","Conversation difficult; privacy impossible","Conversational privacy improves"],"targetsEn":[["Seating layout","Backing onto something solid (hedge, wall) is more private than backing onto open space"],["Masking strategy","Use a continuous low-level source to break a continuous row of seats into small acoustic units"]],"whyEn":"A street soundscape is not better the quieter it is. What restaurant spill-out genuinely needs is the privacy of a conversation that cannot be overheard by the next table, and that can be achieved precisely by introducing continuous water sound. This is a completely different objective from noise reduction.","howEn":"Use soundscape as a space-dividing tool: a curtain of continuous water or canopy wind sound breaks a continuous row of seats into small acoustic units so conversation in one does not disturb the next — essentially cafe acoustics transplanted onto the street. In layout, the side backed by something solid is inherently more private.","watchEn":"An excessively loud masker damages conversation instead (signal-to-noise imbalance); calibrate by measurement.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Plaza GLT 声景更新"]},"材质声":{"unit":"dB(A)","desc":"人行走、触碰不同材质时产生的声音，是「听到的空间」，也是场所气质的一部分。","ranges":[["木 / 竹铺装","足音低沉短促，耐受度高","ok"],["碎石 / 砂砾","足音明显，可承担提示作用（区分路径与边界）","ok"],["金属格栅","高频清脆，靠近住宅区易扰民","warn"],["抛光石材（湿）","足音与滑倒风险同时上升","warn"]],"targets":[["无障碍用途","用材质声差异标记路径与边界（与盲道互补）"],["居住敏感区","避免大面积金属与硬质高反射铺装"]],"why":"材质声常被完全忽略，但它是「可听的地面信息」—— 视障使用者很大程度靠足音判断脚下是什么，这也是「无障碍多感官设计」中触觉与听觉最显著的实证来源。","how":"把材质声当作信息层来用：不同功能区用不同足音（木 / 石 / 碎石）给出可听提示；住宅侧避免金属格栅与大面积硬质；湿滑敏感处优先选有声但不刺耳的材料。与「粗糙度与足底反馈」是一对（一个管触觉、一个管听觉），应联合选材。","watch":"材质声在雨天会显著改变（湿滑、吸声），设计时要把雨天当作「第二模式」一并考虑。","cases":["南京玄武湖无障碍花园"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"dB(A)","titleEn":"Material Sound","descEn":"The sound people make walking on and touching different materials. This is the heard space, and part of a place's character.","rangesEn":["Soft, short footfall; well tolerated","Audible footfall; can carry a warning function","High, bright; can disturb nearby housing","Footfall and slip risk rise together"],"targetsEn":[["Accessibility use","Use differences in material sound to mark routes and boundaries, complementing tactile paving"],["Noise-sensitive areas","Avoid large areas of metal grating and hard reflective paving"]],"whyEn":"Material sound is routinely ignored, yet it is audible ground information — visually impaired users judge what is underfoot largely by footfall sound. This is also the empirical basis for the finding that touch and hearing are the most salient dimensions of accessible multisensory design.","howEn":"Treat material sound as an information layer: give different functional zones different footfall sounds (timber, stone, gravel) as audible cues; avoid metal grating and extensive hard paving on the residential side; where slipperiness is a concern, prefer materials that sound but do not pierce. It pairs with roughness and underfoot feedback — one handles touch, the other hearing — so materials should be selected jointly.","watchEn":"Material sound changes markedly in rain (wet, absorbent). Design should treat the wet state as a second operating mode.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["南京玄武湖无障碍花园"]},"色彩与温度的心理关联":{"unit":"—","desc":"暖色与冷色引起的温度错觉。它不改变任何物理温度，但影响体感与行为。","ranges":[["暖色（红、橙、黄）","主观温度感偏高，约相当于 +1–3 ℃ 的心理感受","warn"],["冷色（蓝、青、绿）","主观温度感偏低，约相当于 −1–3 ℃","ok"],["彩度越高","心理温度效应越强","info"],["夏季停留区大面积高彩度暖色","加剧热感，不建议用于地面与坐面","bad"]],"targets":[["夏季停留区","以冷色 / 中性色为主，避免大面积暖色"],["冬季停留区","可用暖色收拢体感（与加热设施同向协同）"]],"why":"这是「零能耗的体感调节」—— 不改变任何物理量，却能改变人对同一温度的判读。代价只是一桶涂料，因此在成本受限时性价比极高。","how":"把色彩当作热微环境的心理配重：夏季停留区（座椅、遮荫下）用冷色系与中性色，冬季日照区用暖色系，让两侧的体感差被色彩放大。要注意彩度往往比色相影响更大 —— 高明度低彩度的冷色比饱和深蓝更「凉」。与物理降温（遮荫、蒸发）叠加时，心理效应与物理效应同向，收益可叠加。","watch":"心理温度效应存在显著的个体与文化差异（生长环境、个人经历），不能按统一系数设计；对气候响应而言它是补充而非替代。","cases":["喀什「气候—文化双响应」色彩规划"],"srcs":[["气候与文化双响应 —— 以喀什城市色彩规划为例","http://color.fashioncolor.org.cn/CN/PDF/450"]],"unitEn":"—","titleEn":"Colour and Perceived Temperature","descEn":"The temperature illusion created by warm and cool colours. It changes no physical temperature, but it affects felt comfort and behaviour.","rangesEn":["Subjective warmth is higher, roughly equivalent to +1–3 °C in felt terms","Subjective warmth is lower, roughly equivalent to −1–3 °C","The stronger the effect","Intensifies the sense of heat; not recommended for ground or seat surfaces"],"targetsEn":[["Summer seating areas","Lead with cool and neutral tones; avoid large warm areas"],["Winter seating areas","Warm tones can consolidate felt warmth, working with heating in the same direction"]],"whyEn":"This is zero-energy comfort adjustment: it changes no physical quantity yet shifts how people read the same temperature. The cost is one tin of paint, which makes it extremely good value when budgets are tight.","howEn":"Use colour as a psychological counterweight in the thermal microclimate: cool and neutral tones in summer seating areas (seats, shaded zones), warm tones in winter sunny zones, so colour amplifies the felt difference between the two. Note that chroma often matters more than hue — a light, low-chroma cool tone reads cooler than a saturated deep blue. Where it stacks with physical cooling (shade, evaporation), the psychological and physical effects run the same way and the gains add up.","watchEn":"The effect varies significantly between individuals and cultures (upbringing, personal experience), so it cannot be designed to a fixed coefficient. For climate response it is a supplement, not a substitute.","srcsEn":["Climate and culture dual response: urban colour planning in Kashgar"],"casesEn":["喀什「气候—文化双响应」色彩规划"]},"彩度造成的空间感知差":{"unit":"—","desc":"高彩度色块在视觉上显得更近、更小、更活跃；低彩度显得更远、更开阔、更平静。这是用色彩调整空间感受的手段。","ranges":[["高彩度","前进感，视觉上拉近距离，空间显小","warn"],["低彩度","后退感，空间显得开阔","ok"],["同类色深浅交替","可制造节奏而不增加彩度负担","ok"]],"targets":[["狭窄街段","用低彩度降低压迫感"],["需要强调的节点","局部高彩度，面积控制在 5–10 %"]],"why":"色彩是唯一能在不改变任何尺寸的情况下改变「空间感」的手段 —— 对不能拆改的既有街道，这是最廉价的空间调节工具。","how":"按三段式配方控制：基底（低彩度，占 70 % 以上）→ 辅助（中彩度，20–25 %）→ 点缀（高彩度，≤10 %）。苏州十全街的教训正是点缀占比失控 —— 商户各自发挥导致高彩度面积过大，与街区基准色冲突。街道色彩管控的实质，是管控高彩度的总面积，而不是禁色。","watch":"色彩评价带强文化与个体差异；历史街区的基准色应实测取得（测色仪采样），不能凭印象定。","cases":["苏州十全街商业色彩评价","喀什「气候—文化双响应」色彩规划"],"srcs":[["Commercial colour impact on traditional heritage features, Suzhou Shiquan historic district (Nature HSSC 2025)","https://www.nature.com/articles/s40494-025-01905-6"]],"unitEn":"—","titleEn":"Chroma and Spatial Perception","descEn":"High-chroma patches read as closer, smaller and more active; low-chroma as further, more open and calmer. This is how colour adjusts the perception of space.","rangesEn":["Advancing; visually pulls closer and makes the space feel smaller","Receding; the space feels more open","Creates rhythm without adding chroma load"],"targetsEn":[["Narrow street segments","Use low chroma to reduce compression"],["Nodes needing emphasis","Limited high chroma, kept to 5–10 % of area"]],"whyEn":"Colour is the only means of changing how large a space feels without changing any dimension. For existing streets that cannot be demolished, it is the cheapest spatial adjustment available.","howEn":"Work to a three-part ratio: base (low chroma, over 70 %), secondary (medium chroma, 20–25 %), accent (high chroma, ≤10 %). The lesson from Suzhou's Shiquan Street is precisely that the accent share ran out of control — every shopfront improvising pushed high-chroma area too far and conflicted with the district base palette. Colour control on a street is really control of total high-chroma area, not a ban on colour.","watchEn":"Colour evaluation is strongly cultural and individual. Base colours for a historic district should be measured on site with a colorimeter, not set from impression.","srcsEn":["Commercial colour impact on traditional heritage features, Suzhou Shiquan historic district (Nature HSSC 2025)"],"casesEn":["苏州十全街商业色彩评价","喀什「气候—文化双响应」色彩规划"]},"地面色彩分区":{"unit":"—","desc":"用铺装色彩差异标示功能分区与通行路径，替代或补充标识牌。是街道中面积最大、最容易被忽略的信息载体。","ranges":[["色差 ΔE > 5","可被明显识别（NCS / CIELAB 体系）","ok"],["色差 ΔE 2–5","需仔细辨认，适合细微提示","warn"],["仅靠明度差","在弱光与色觉障碍人群中最可靠","ok"],["明度差 <30 %","色觉障碍人群难以识别","bad"]],"targets":[["路径引导","主通道用连续同色，支路与停留区做区分"],["无障碍兼容","关键分界的明度差 ≥30 %"]],"why":"地面本就是信息载体，用色彩分区几乎不增加造价（本来就要铺装），却能把「哪里该走、哪里可停」直接写进材料。","how":"三层用法：① 通行带用连续、低彩度、明度稳定的铺装，形成稳定导引；② 停留与活动区换色换质（色彩与粗糙度同步变化，同时作用于视觉与足底）；③ 注意明度优先于色相 —— 因为色觉障碍人群（约 8 % 男性）主要依赖明度差，而弱光与雨天会让色相差异迅速失效。与 C3.2 地面导视是同一件事的两种尺度。","watch":"色彩与粗糙度同步变化时，可能给轮椅与推车带来额外阻力，通行带上须保持一致。","cases":["喀什「气候—文化双响应」色彩规划"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"—","titleEn":"Ground Colour Zoning","descEn":"Using differences in paving colour to mark functional zones and circulation routes, replacing or supplementing signage. The largest and most overlooked information carrier on a street.","rangesEn":["Clearly identifiable (NCS / CIELAB)","Needs close attention; suited to subtle cues","The most reliable approach in low light and for people with colour vision deficiency","Hard to identify for people with colour vision deficiency"],"targetsEn":[["Route guidance","Continuous same colour on the main route; differentiate branches and resting areas"],["Accessibility compatibility","At least 30 % lightness difference at key boundaries"]],"whyEn":"Ground is already an information carrier. Colour zoning adds almost no cost, since paving is needed anyway, yet it writes where to walk and where to stop directly into the material.","howEn":"Three layers. (1) Continuous, low-chroma, lightness-stable paving on circulation corridors gives stable guidance. (2) Resting and activity areas change colour and texture together, acting on both vision and the sole of the foot. (3) Put lightness before hue, because people with colour vision deficiency (about 8 % of men) rely mainly on lightness differences, and low light or rain quickly defeats hue differences. This is the same idea as ground wayfinding at a different scale.","watchEn":"Where colour and roughness change together, wheelchairs and trolleys meet extra resistance; keep circulation corridors consistent.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["喀什「气候—文化双响应」色彩规划"]},"恢复性环境效益":{"unit":"min","desc":"多感官自然环境对压力恢复与注意力恢复的可测量效益，是「为什么小干预也有效」的实证基础。","ranges":[["30 min × 4 次暴露","唾液皮质醇 −18.6 %、幸福感 +10.2 %、自评产出 +5.4 %","ok"],["单次 10–20 min","已有可测的情绪指标改善","ok"],["无障碍多感官花园（n = 48）","多感官体验与生活质量的相关系数 r = 0.460（p = 0.001）","ok"],["解释力","多感官体验与使用可达性可解释生活质量方差的 26.3 %","info"]],"targets":[["配置门槛","街区至少一处 10 min 可达的多感官停留点"],["设计原则","统一 / 尺度 / 平衡 / 简洁 / 多样 / 序列 / 多感官参与（七原则）"]],"why":"这是把「体感」从主观陈述变成可测指标的证据链 —— 皮质醇是生理指标、幸福感是量表指标，两者在同一实验里同时改善，说明多感官设计的作用可被验证，而不只是「感觉良好」。","how":"两条可操作结论：① 「暴露时长不必长」—— 4 次 × 30 分钟就足够测出变化，说明街道级的短时暴露有效，不必追求城市公园的尺度；② 「七原则中的序列与简洁最关键」—— 不是刺激越多越好。这为小干预提供了理论许可：与其做一处大而全的景观，不如沿街布若干处小而有序列的感官点。","watch":"多数研究样本量偏小（n = 48 这类），且以特定人群为主（老人、视障者），向一般人群外推需谨慎。","cases":["Souter-Brown 感官花园对照实验","南京玄武湖无障碍花园"],"srcs":[["Urban Greenery for Health — Sensory Gardens and Improved Well-Being (Souter-Brown, Routledge 2025)","https://www.taylorfrancis.com/chapters/edit/10.4324/9781003344285-16/urban-greenery-health-gayle-souter-brown"],["Accessible Multisensory Garden and Its Impact on Quality of Life among Elderly Residents (Pertanika 2025)","http://www.pertanika.upm.edu.my/resources/files/Pertanika%20PAPERS/PP%20Vol.%201%20(6)%202025/PP(6)-009-2025.pdf"]],"unitEn":"min","titleEn":"Restorative Benefit","descEn":"The measurable benefit of multisensory natural environments for stress recovery and attention restoration — the evidential basis for why small interventions work.","rangesEn":["Salivary cortisol −18.6 %, well-being +10.2 %, self-rated output +5.4 %","Measurable emotional improvement already present","Correlation between multisensory experience and quality of life r = 0.460 (p = 0.001)","Multisensory experience plus access usability explain 26.3 % of the variance in quality of life"],"targetsEn":[["Provision threshold","At least one multisensory resting point within 10 min of the street"],["Design principles","Unity, human-centred scale, balance, simplicity, biodiversity, sequence, multisensory engagement"]],"whyEn":"This is the evidential chain that turns felt experience from a subjective claim into a measurable indicator. Cortisol is a physiological marker and well-being a scale score, and both improved in the same study — so multisensory design can be verified rather than merely asserted.","howEn":"Two operational conclusions. (1) Exposure need not be long: four 30-minute sessions were enough to detect change, so street-scale short exposure works and there is no need to aim for a city-park scale. (2) Of the seven principles, sequence and simplicity matter most — more stimulus is not better. This gives theoretical permission for small interventions: rather than one large all-encompassing landscape, place several small, sequenced sensory points along the street.","watchEn":"Most studies have small samples (n = 48 and similar) and focus on specific groups (older adults, visually impaired users); extrapolation to the general population needs caution.","srcsEn":["Urban Greenery for Health — Sensory Gardens and Improved Well-Being (Souter-Brown, Routledge 2025)","Accessible Multisensory Garden and Its Impact on Quality of Life among Elderly Residents (Pertanika 2025)"],"casesEn":["Souter-Brown 感官花园对照实验","南京玄武湖无障碍花园"]},"感官补偿与相加 / 相消":{"unit":"—","desc":"多感官同时受刺激时，总体验不等于各感官之和 —— 可能相互增强（相加），也可能相互削弱（相消）。","ranges":[["同向感官叠加（荫 + 风 + 湿）","体感改善大于单项之和","ok"],["一好一坏并存（清凉但嘈杂）","整体评价常被坏项主导","bad"],["感官冲突（噪声叠加高温）","主观不适增幅超单项叠加","bad"],["小剂量多感官（各给一点）","优于单感官给足","ok"]],"targets":[["配置原则","优先消除短板，再叠加长板"],["多感官配比","每项给到可辨识即止，不追求单项极致"]],"why":"这条直接决定预算该怎么花。人对环境的评价常被最差的感官维度拽住，所以把资源投在「消除最差的那一项」，收益远大于把某一项做到极致。","how":"两步走：① 「先补短板」—— 如果街段噪声超标，再漂亮的色彩与香气也留不住人，应先做声景；② 「再做多感官小幅叠加」—— 短板补齐后加入气味、触感、光影的小剂量改善，让体验从「能待」变成「想待」。这也解释了蒙特利尔雾森广场第三版为何失败：水景尺度失配，把一个潜在的正面感官变成了新的负面项（相消）。","watch":"感官相消的阈值难以预测，需现场试用（C7.1 原型上街试用）验证，不能只靠图纸推演。","cases":["蒙特利尔三版雾森广场","上海「脑迷宫」花园"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"—","titleEn":"Sensory Addition and Cancellation","descEn":"When several senses are stimulated at once, the total experience is not the sum of the parts — they can reinforce one another (addition) or cancel each other out (subtraction).","rangesEn":["Felt improvement exceeds the sum of the parts","Overall appraisal is usually dominated by the bad item","Subjective discomfort rises more than the sum of the parts","Better than saturating one sense"],"targetsEn":[["Configuration principle","Remove the weakest link first, then stack the strengths"],["Multisensory ratio","Give each sense enough to be discernible and stop there; do not maximise any one"]],"whyEn":"This decides how the budget should be spent. People's appraisal of an environment is usually dragged down by the worst sensory dimension, so money spent removing the worst item returns far more than money spent perfecting one item.","howEn":"Two steps. (1) Fix the weakest link first: if the segment exceeds noise limits, no amount of colour or scent will hold people, so start with the soundscape. (2) Then add small multisensory layers: once the weak link is resolved, add small doses of scent, touch and light so the experience moves from habitable to desirable. This also explains why the third iteration of the Montreal mister plaza failed — the water feature was the wrong scale, converting a potential positive sense into a new negative one.","watchEn":"The threshold at which senses cancel each other is hard to predict and needs on-site trials (prototyping in the street) rather than drawing-board reasoning.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Montreal Three Misters Square","上海「脑迷宫」花园"]},"感官冲突":{"unit":"—","desc":"两个胁迫因子同时作用于不同感官时产生的放大效应，如「噪声 + 高温」的不适感明显大于两者单独叠加。","ranges":[["噪声 + 高温","主观不适增幅超单项之和（环境中较弱的一维被更严厉评价）","bad"],["眩光 + 高温","视觉不适与热感互相放大","bad"],["气味 + 高湿","闷味感知被放大","warn"],["单因子达标但另一因子超标","整体评价仍以超标项为准","warn"]],"targets":[["设计校核","不得只校核单一因子，需做组合工况评估"],["优先序","先处理冲突最强的组合（声 + 热、光 + 热）"]],"why":"街道设计常按单个因子分工校核（声学一组、热工一组），但使用者承受的是组合结果。实测研究显示，当环境中某一维度较弱时，人会对它作出更严厉的评价 —— 短板不是被平均，而是被放大。","how":"建立组合工况意识：把噪声与热、眩光与热这两组最常见的冲突单独列为校核项，在方案阶段就检查是否会出现「一好一坏」的组合（如为降温加的高反射铺装造成眩光、为遮荫种的密植乔木困住污染物）。做法上优先选同向收益的措施 —— 树冠同时管遮荫、降噪、滞尘、降风速，是冲突最小的一类。","watch":"组合效应的量化模型尚不成熟，多数结论来自实验室与问卷，现场标定仍需实测。","cases":["蒙特利尔三版雾森广场","苏州十全街商业色彩评价"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"—","titleEn":"Sensory Conflict","descEn":"The amplification that occurs when two stressors act on different senses at once — noise plus heat feels markedly worse than the sum of the two alone.","rangesEn":["Subjective discomfort rises more than the sum of the parts; the weaker dimension is judged more harshly","Visual discomfort and felt heat amplify each other","Perception of stuffiness is amplified","Overall appraisal still follows the item that is over the limit"],"targetsEn":[["Design check","Do not check single factors only; assess combined conditions"],["Priority","Address the strongest conflicts first (sound plus heat, light plus heat)"]],"whyEn":"Street design is usually checked factor by factor, with one team on acoustics and another on thermal performance, but what users endure is the combination. Measured studies show that when one dimension of an environment is weak, people judge it more harshly — the weakest link is not averaged out, it is amplified.","howEn":"Build combined-condition awareness: list noise with heat and glare with heat as separate check items, and at scheme stage examine whether a good-plus-bad combination arises — high-reflectance paving added for cooling causing glare, or densely planted trees added for shade trapping pollutants. In practice, favour measures with same-direction benefits: a tree canopy handles shade, noise attenuation, dust interception and wind speed at once, which makes it the least conflicting option.","watchEn":"Quantitative models of combined effects are still immature; most findings come from laboratories and questionnaires, and on-site calibration still requires measurement.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["Montreal Three Misters Square","苏州十全街商业色彩评价"]},"感官敏感人群差异":{"unit":"—","desc":"不同人群对气味、声音、光、触感的敏感度差异极大，设计需为「受不了」的人保留回避路径。","ranges":[["气味敏感（哮喘、偏头痛）","浓香可诱发不适，容忍度远低于常人","warn"],["声音敏感（听觉过敏、自闭谱系）","高频与突发声尤其难受","warn"],["光敏感（偏头痛、白化症）","眩光与强对比最为不利","warn"],["色觉障碍（约 8 % 男性）","主要依赖明度差而非色相差","warn"],["老年人","中性温度更高，需要更暖的微环境","info"]],"targets":[["配置原则","每个感官刺激都应配套一条「绕开」的路径"],["强度控制","把刺激源放在路径一侧，而非路径正中"]],"why":"多感官设计有一个内在风险：刺激越丰富，越可能伤到最敏感的那部分人。而一旦一个空间对某些人「进不去」，它就失去了公共性 —— 这与无障碍是同一个命题。","how":"把「回避」当成设计要素而不是补救：芳香植物种在路径一侧（另一侧留无障碍通道与座椅）、声源与座位保持 3 m 以上距离并保留安静区、高彩度只用于节点而非通路。成果应能用一句话检验：「如果我对气味（声音 / 光）很敏感，还能不能穿过这段街道并坐下来？」","watch":"敏感度阈值缺乏统一标准，个体差异极大，宜用现场问卷而非指标推断；不要用「只是少数人」为理由跳过这一步。","cases":["南京玄武湖无障碍花园","上海「脑迷宫」花园"],"srcs":[],"unitEn":"—","titleEn":"Sensory Sensitivity Differences","descEn":"Sensitivity to smell, sound, light and touch varies enormously between people. Design must preserve an avoidance route for those who cannot tolerate it.","rangesEn":["Strong scent can trigger discomfort; tolerance far below average","High-frequency and sudden sounds are especially difficult","Glare and strong contrast are the most adverse","Rely mainly on lightness rather than hue difference","Neutral temperature is higher; a warmer microclimate is needed"],"targetsEn":[["Configuration principle","Every sensory stimulus should come with a route around it"],["Intensity control","Put the stimulus to one side of the route, not in the middle of it"]],"whyEn":"Multisensory design carries an inherent risk: the richer the stimulus, the more likely it is to harm the most sensitive users. And once a space becomes inaccessible to some people it loses its publicness — the same proposition as accessibility.","howEn":"Treat avoidance as a design element rather than a remedy: plant aromatic species on one side of the route and keep an accessible corridor and seating on the other; keep sound sources at least 3 m from seats and retain a quiet zone; reserve high chroma for nodes rather than thoroughfares. The outcome should pass a one-sentence test: if I am highly sensitive to scent (sound, light), can I still cross this street and sit down?","watchEn":"Sensitivity thresholds lack a common standard and vary enormously between individuals; use on-site questionnaires rather than inferred indices, and do not skip this step on the grounds that it concerns only a few people.","srcsEn":[],"casesEn":["南京玄武湖无障碍花园","上海「脑迷宫」花园"]}};
